1
00:02:03,469 --> 00:02:10,879
Visit turkision.com for more!

2
00:02:11,767 --> 00:02:12,921
What are you saying, Yakup Bey?

3
00:02:41,623 --> 00:02:42,519
Yakup Bey!

4
00:02:44,059 --> 00:02:45,257
What are you doing?

5
00:02:46,503 --> 00:02:47,457
You let my prey escape!

6
00:02:48,034 --> 00:02:48,615
Today...

7
00:02:51,548 --> 00:02:52,916
you are the prey.

8
00:02:54,316 --> 00:02:55,670
And I am the hunter, Osman!

9
00:03:03,091 --> 00:03:04,128
Isn't there news from Vasilis?

10
00:03:04,928 --> 00:03:06,294
He still hasn't left the border market,
Master.

11
00:03:08,461 --> 00:03:09,820
Yakup is taking precaution.

12
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:12,479
The old wolf thinks of all possibilities.

13
00:03:12,746 --> 00:03:14,211
Well, what are you thinking of doing?

14
00:03:15,144 --> 00:03:16,634
We'll take Vasilis out of there.

15
00:03:17,167 --> 00:03:18,253
Let him come...

16
00:03:28,042 --> 00:03:30,352
You planned a real good game,
right, Crusader?

17
00:03:31,354 --> 00:03:33,424
Now Yakup and Osman
are against one another.

18
00:03:33,924 --> 00:03:35,739
They'll drown in their own blood.

19
00:03:37,872 --> 00:03:38,886
But...

20
00:03:39,953 --> 00:03:41,064
I don't trust the game...

21
00:03:41,497 --> 00:03:42,675
I trust my sword.

22
00:03:44,942 --> 00:03:47,736
Send word to the soldiers
to surround the Inn!

23
00:03:55,417 --> 00:03:56,590
After you...

24
00:03:57,257 --> 00:03:58,882
I will kill that dog too.

25
00:04:00,549 --> 00:04:02,959
It's not about getting rid of
the enemy.

26
00:04:03,492 --> 00:04:05,256
Rather the traitor among us...

27
00:04:05,756 --> 00:04:07,991
we must get rid of them!

28
00:04:08,591 --> 00:04:09,419
Yakup Bey!

29
00:04:12,952 --> 00:04:14,451
You're testing my patience.

30
00:04:17,317 --> 00:04:18,660
But I can't hold it back anymore.

31
00:04:20,127 --> 00:04:21,089
Your betrayal...

32
00:04:21,755 --> 00:04:23,240
has been exposed, Osman.

33
00:04:25,207 --> 00:04:26,749
You will answer now.

34
00:04:27,446 --> 00:04:28,792
You will die!

35
00:04:29,325 --> 00:04:31,287
I have nothing to answer to you for...

36
00:04:31,786 --> 00:04:33,195
nor do I owe you my life!

37
00:04:37,182 --> 00:04:39,244
I waited until now for peace.

38
00:04:39,611 --> 00:04:40,696
But now it's over.

39
00:04:43,215 --> 00:04:46,227
Today, only one of us will leave here alive.

40
00:04:47,460 --> 00:04:49,164
Let's see who that will be...

41
00:04:50,864 --> 00:04:52,430
Yakup Bey!

42
00:05:00,910 --> 00:05:02,834
You knew the punishment for betrayal.

43
00:05:03,467 --> 00:05:04,554
You did this knowingly.

44
00:05:05,054 --> 00:05:06,983
Now it's time to pay the price!

45
00:05:07,316 --> 00:05:09,580
I said you wouldn't open your eyes
before falling into negligence.

46
00:05:10,115 --> 00:05:12,555
But it seems you won't open
your eyes before dying.

47
00:05:14,722 --> 00:05:15,701
Tell me.

48
00:05:16,034 --> 00:05:17,200
With whose words did you come here?

49
00:05:17,633 --> 00:05:18,771
With which dog's words?

50
00:05:19,238 --> 00:05:20,447
Your Alp, Veysel!

51
00:05:24,723 --> 00:05:25,538
Veysel?

52
00:05:25,804 --> 00:05:27,299
Veysel is the traitor in my palace.

53
00:05:27,599 --> 00:05:28,695
Bayındır was after him.

54
00:05:29,233 --> 00:05:31,433
Do you came and face me
with the words of a traitor?

55
00:05:48,677 --> 00:05:50,621
We have been dealing with
them for so long.

56
00:05:50,854 --> 00:05:52,503
You couldn't walk the path even a little.

57
00:05:52,770 --> 00:05:54,262
Do you still fall for their games?

58
00:05:54,595 --> 00:05:57,412
We didn't learn the game from
infidels like you did, Osman.

59
00:05:57,985 --> 00:06:00,506
They came before us,
and we crushed them.

60
00:06:00,956 --> 00:06:02,925
But you learnt to betray from them.

61
00:06:04,434 --> 00:06:05,456
What's your proof?

62
00:06:05,679 --> 00:06:08,827
The Mongol poison was
brought from your palace.

63
00:06:09,193 --> 00:06:12,033
The poison that poisoned
my daughter Gonca.

64
00:06:16,104 --> 00:06:17,581
They plot their games in such a way...

65
00:06:18,048 --> 00:06:19,535
it's impossible not to believe it.

66
00:06:19,902 --> 00:06:21,034
There's no game.

67
00:06:22,267 --> 00:06:23,853
I was always right, Osman.

68
00:06:33,741 --> 00:06:35,088
They always was a game.

69
00:06:35,521 --> 00:06:36,979
But you were always wrong.

70
00:06:38,566 --> 00:06:39,282
Alps!

71
00:06:39,782 --> 00:06:41,102
Leave the Germiyans!

72
00:06:42,854 --> 00:06:44,025
Turn to the heathens!

73
00:06:53,766 --> 00:06:56,043
Alps! Kill the Mongols!

74
00:07:24,501 --> 00:07:27,359
You're going to ruin my meticulously
planned game with this attack!

75
00:07:28,626 --> 00:07:29,673
The game is yours.

76
00:07:30,073 --> 00:07:31,342
The war is ours, crusader.

77
00:07:34,535 --> 00:07:36,524
While they're both inside,
I won't stand still.

78
00:07:37,121 --> 00:07:39,192
You will be the cause of them uniting!

79
00:07:45,004 --> 00:07:46,651
Let that scare you, crusader.

80
00:07:47,118 --> 00:07:47,938
I...

81
00:07:48,571 --> 00:07:51,714
am the servant of Olcaytu Han,
and soldier of Emir Çoban.

82
00:07:53,095 --> 00:07:55,965
I am the link that holds their state
together with taxes.

83
00:08:01,890 --> 00:08:05,575
Together or separate, it makes no difference.

84
00:08:07,342 --> 00:08:09,533
I am their executioner.

85
00:08:22,527 --> 00:08:25,369
If they were to go down fighting,
we would have made them fall.

86
00:08:26,785 --> 00:08:28,515
You will be in need of my games...

87
00:08:29,382 --> 00:08:30,142
Mongols.

88
00:08:35,208 --> 00:08:37,929
Master, everything was done
as you commanded.

89
00:08:38,328 --> 00:08:39,780
Our men are waiting at the border market.

90
00:08:40,448 --> 00:08:41,037
Good.

91
00:08:42,370 --> 00:08:43,164
Let's go.

92
00:08:45,097 --> 00:08:46,535
There's nothing left to do here.

93
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,015
Hold the entrances.

94
00:09:36,131 --> 00:09:38,491
My Bey, these dogs keep coming.

95
00:09:38,824 --> 00:09:40,771
You leave. I'll come after you.

96
00:09:44,880 --> 00:09:45,980
Be careful, son.

97
00:09:46,326 --> 00:09:47,965
- Be careful.
- Don't worry, my Bey.

98
00:09:48,383 --> 00:09:49,110
Konur.

99
00:09:50,242 --> 00:09:52,047
We'll leave from the back door.

100
00:09:53,652 --> 00:09:54,811
Yakup Bey.

101
00:09:55,660 --> 00:09:56,407
Come on.

102
00:09:57,642 --> 00:09:58,714
Come on, son.

103
00:09:58,914 --> 00:09:59,625
Come on.

104
00:10:07,932 --> 00:10:09,649
The dog that shows its teeth to the wolf...

105
00:10:10,590 --> 00:10:11,504
ends up dead.

106
00:10:12,734 --> 00:10:13,495
Alps.

107
00:10:14,288 --> 00:10:15,582
Release the doors.

108
00:10:17,158 --> 00:10:18,754
Your teeth can't do anything to me.

109
00:10:19,360 --> 00:10:21,481
But I will ruin you all.

110
00:10:26,058 --> 00:10:28,958
GERMIYANOĞLU BORDER / BORDER MARKET

111
00:10:39,870 --> 00:10:40,865
Take this. Eat. You shouldn't die.

112
00:10:43,259 --> 00:10:43,956
Give me.

113
00:10:45,495 --> 00:10:46,255
Give me.

114
00:11:10,763 --> 00:11:12,934
It's time for you to get out of the cage.

115
00:11:13,335 --> 00:11:16,689
Jesus' loyal soldiers are coming for you.

116
00:11:16,889 --> 00:11:17,460
Get ready.

117
00:11:17,882 --> 00:11:19,033
Master.

118
00:11:25,392 --> 00:11:26,608
Saadet Hatun!

119
00:11:28,217 --> 00:11:29,287
Yakup Bey!

120
00:11:30,154 --> 00:11:31,286
Come outside!

121
00:11:35,826 --> 00:11:36,919
Saadet Hatun!

122
00:11:38,517 --> 00:11:39,736
Who am I talking to?

123
00:11:41,652 --> 00:11:42,840
Get out of my way!

124
00:11:46,015 --> 00:11:47,044
Ülgen, where is my son?

125
00:11:47,311 --> 00:11:48,123
Bala Hatun.

126
00:11:48,419 --> 00:11:50,215
Your son is in the prison, Bala.

127
00:11:51,215 --> 00:11:52,735
Until Yakup Bey comes...

128
00:11:53,035 --> 00:11:54,016
he is under arrest.

129
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:55,291
Saadet Hatun.

130
00:11:55,591 --> 00:11:57,342
I want my son and my Alps.

131
00:12:00,435 --> 00:12:02,165
You probably didn't hear me.

132
00:12:06,338 --> 00:12:07,966
Until Yakup Bey comes...

133
00:12:08,366 --> 00:12:09,578
they are all under arrest.

134
00:12:10,011 --> 00:12:11,068
For what reason?

135
00:12:11,701 --> 00:12:12,848
What is their crime?

136
00:12:13,251 --> 00:12:15,367
You will find out when Yakup Bey comes.

137
00:12:23,289 --> 00:12:27,349
Saadet Hatun, your scales of justice
have lost balance.

138
00:12:28,964 --> 00:12:30,525
Alaeddin has committed no crime.

139
00:12:30,927 --> 00:12:33,673
I will not allow you to imprison
my son for no reason.

140
00:12:33,913 --> 00:12:34,845
Alps!

141
00:12:46,729 --> 00:12:49,560
This is my land.

142
00:12:52,561 --> 00:12:57,639
Just as I was your guest
in your palace...

143
00:12:58,739 --> 00:13:03,305
now your son and your Alps
are my guests.

144
00:13:05,964 --> 00:13:07,671
You want reprisal, huh?

145
00:13:09,520 --> 00:13:10,583
Not at all.

146
00:13:11,133 --> 00:13:13,324
My intention is very sincere.

147
00:13:16,295 --> 00:13:17,627
Your son and your Alps...

148
00:13:18,460 --> 00:13:20,196
are my guests...

149
00:13:21,196 --> 00:13:23,277
until Yakup Bey comes.

150
00:13:31,212 --> 00:13:32,629
Since you say your intention is sincere...

151
00:13:34,857 --> 00:13:36,348
then release my Alps.

152
00:13:36,815 --> 00:13:38,166
You have no problem with them.

153
00:13:43,707 --> 00:13:44,944
I will be the better person.

154
00:13:45,891 --> 00:13:47,491
Your Alps are free.

155
00:13:49,958 --> 00:13:51,255
Now, Bala Hatun...

156
00:13:52,222 --> 00:13:53,005
go.

157
00:13:53,405 --> 00:13:54,243
No.

158
00:13:54,798 --> 00:13:57,200
Until my son is released...

159
00:13:57,400 --> 00:13:58,897
I will stay right here, Saadet Hatun.

160
00:14:01,097 --> 00:14:03,227
You won't stand still, Bala.
I know.

161
00:14:07,127 --> 00:14:08,052
But...

162
00:14:08,419 --> 00:14:11,725
leave my market now.

163
00:14:13,114 --> 00:14:16,890
I won't go anywhere without taking my son.

164
00:14:21,310 --> 00:14:23,238
Since this is your land...

165
00:14:24,638 --> 00:14:25,793
...what are you afraid of?

166
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:29,981
Then you will stay...

167
00:14:30,863 --> 00:14:32,488
and your Alps will go

168
00:14:52,975 --> 00:14:54,200
Alps, be careful.

169
00:14:54,733 --> 00:14:56,508
These Mongols aren't like the others.

170
00:14:57,630 --> 00:14:59,980
We are suffering because
of your mistakes.

171
00:15:00,758 --> 00:15:04,196
You brought the Mongols upon us
before we could even get on our feet.

172
00:15:04,629 --> 00:15:06,718
What you call a mistake is the fire
of the independence of the Turks.

173
00:15:07,885 --> 00:15:09,060
Yes, I brought them upon us...

174
00:15:10,010 --> 00:15:11,441
but I didn't give them a good time.

175
00:15:12,574 --> 00:15:13,276
Osman.

176
00:15:17,607 --> 00:15:18,272
Alps!

177
00:16:54,466 --> 00:16:56,558
There's no escape from my might.

178
00:16:56,758 --> 00:16:58,641
You will feel my wrath now!

179
00:16:59,011 --> 00:17:01,440
You bring your wrath on the oppressed.

180
00:17:01,940 --> 00:17:03,901
But we are the protectors
of the oppressed.

181
00:17:04,934 --> 00:17:08,505
And our wrath will fall on all
the oppressors!

182
00:17:09,047 --> 00:17:09,714
You'll see.

183
00:17:10,349 --> 00:17:11,060
Come on, Boran!

184
00:17:11,560 --> 00:17:13,656
- Allah is the Greatest!
- O Right!

185
00:17:17,759 --> 00:17:18,898
Ya Allah!

186
00:17:21,444 --> 00:17:24,829
I will rain death upon you!

187
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:27,948
Today, these lands will
be your graves!

188
00:17:35,687 --> 00:17:36,331
Bala Hatun.

189
00:17:36,721 --> 00:17:38,546
Bayındır Bey and the Alps are now free.

190
00:17:39,496 --> 00:17:40,588
Okay. Good.

191
00:17:46,879 --> 00:17:48,059
Why is this cart in a hurry?

192
00:17:50,042 --> 00:17:50,799
Where is it going?

193
00:17:50,999 --> 00:17:51,747
Hasan...

194
00:17:52,379 --> 00:17:54,666
take some Alps with you and
go after it quickly. Come on.

195
00:17:55,198 --> 00:17:56,080
As you command, Bala Hatun.

196
00:18:05,635 --> 00:18:06,747
Veysel!

197
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:10,723
How did you hide yourself for so long?

198
00:18:11,856 --> 00:18:13,240
How couldn't I see it?

199
00:18:17,525 --> 00:18:19,835
Gonca Hatun. Gonca Hatun.
Gonca Hatun.

200
00:18:21,407 --> 00:18:22,549
Mehmet Bey has strict orders...

201
00:18:23,182 --> 00:18:24,288
we cannot let anyone in.

202
00:18:24,655 --> 00:18:25,701
Am I anyone?

203
00:18:26,468 --> 00:18:27,293
Get out.

204
00:18:34,975 --> 00:18:37,048
Oh, welcome, deceitful Hatun.

205
00:18:47,891 --> 00:18:48,729
Don't look at me like that.

206
00:18:50,662 --> 00:18:52,709
I thought your father wouldn't believe it?

207
00:18:52,736 --> 00:18:54,914
What were you going to do by raiding
my father's tent, Alaeddin Bey ?

208
00:18:56,968 --> 00:18:59,276
My father would've heard
Veysel out either way.

209
00:19:00,206 --> 00:19:01,337
I don't understand, Gonca.

210
00:19:02,737 --> 00:19:04,494
He trusts the word of one man.

211
00:19:06,561 --> 00:19:07,821
Is there someone else?

212
00:19:09,297 --> 00:19:13,053
Osman Bey will go to
someone named Karacelasun.

213
00:19:14,827 --> 00:19:16,185
Their numbers are small.

214
00:19:19,094 --> 00:19:21,033
Alaeddin was going to chart the path.

215
00:19:22,535 --> 00:19:23,253
I don't know.

216
00:19:30,870 --> 00:19:31,598
Does it hurt?

217
00:19:32,657 --> 00:19:33,806
Do you feel guilty?

218
00:19:34,906 --> 00:19:35,868
Or do you pity me?

219
00:19:37,927 --> 00:19:39,701
Why would I feel guilty?

220
00:19:40,968 --> 00:19:41,684
I don't know.

221
00:19:42,817 --> 00:19:44,460
Maybe because your brother did this to me.

222
00:20:02,702 --> 00:20:03,842
I got my answer.

223
00:20:06,434 --> 00:20:07,643
What's the answer?

224
00:20:09,643 --> 00:20:10,923
You couldn't harm me.

225
00:20:16,607 --> 00:20:17,457
Is that so?

226
00:20:18,157 --> 00:20:19,630
Your tongue has no limits.

227
00:20:20,236 --> 00:20:22,623
If you talk like that again,
you'll see how I hurt you.

228
00:20:24,423 --> 00:20:26,022
You're not only deceitful...

229
00:20:26,622 --> 00:20:28,115
you're also heartless.

230
00:20:31,080 --> 00:20:32,424
Heartless Gonca.

231
00:20:35,738 --> 00:20:37,037
Your father believed Veysel.

232
00:20:38,029 --> 00:20:38,852
What about you?

233
00:20:39,619 --> 00:20:40,545
Do you believe him?

234
00:20:43,076 --> 00:20:43,891
I believe you.

235
00:20:47,856 --> 00:20:49,873
And when my father speaks to Osman Bey...

236
00:20:50,106 --> 00:20:51,603
he will surely understand the truth.

237
00:20:53,336 --> 00:20:54,219
Do you...

238
00:20:55,676 --> 00:20:57,026
really trust me?

239
00:21:00,359 --> 00:21:01,308
I do.

240
00:21:06,121 --> 00:21:07,401
Do you trust me?

241
00:21:14,867 --> 00:21:15,651
Gonca?

242
00:21:45,767 --> 00:21:46,879
Allah is the Greatest!

243
00:21:49,012 --> 00:21:49,827
Ya Allah!

244
00:21:56,094 --> 00:21:56,863
Boran Bey...

245
00:21:57,130 --> 00:21:58,835
what will we do when
our arrows run out?

246
00:21:59,144 --> 00:22:01,174
My Bey, all our arrows have run out.

247
00:22:03,120 --> 00:22:03,914
We will wait.

248
00:22:04,455 --> 00:22:05,259
We will wait.

249
00:22:05,526 --> 00:22:06,515
They can't resist.

250
00:22:06,896 --> 00:22:08,681
They have no strength to resist.

251
00:22:09,014 --> 00:22:10,919
Strike them, soldiers of Erlik Han!

252
00:22:16,167 --> 00:22:17,094
Stand together!

253
00:22:26,221 --> 00:22:28,455
Alps! Shoot your arrows!

254
00:22:30,433 --> 00:22:31,179
Son?

255
00:22:33,661 --> 00:22:34,845
Allah is the Greatest!

256
00:22:36,113 --> 00:22:37,380
Allah is the Greatest!

257
00:22:38,822 --> 00:22:41,043
Soldiers, retreat!

258
00:22:42,933 --> 00:22:44,971
I won't die before getting my revenge.

259
00:22:45,606 --> 00:22:47,736
The wrath of the dark spirits
will fall upon you!

260
00:22:50,485 --> 00:22:51,188
Come on!

261
00:22:53,710 --> 00:22:54,529
Come on!

262
00:22:55,328 --> 00:22:56,898
- Ya Allah!
- Ya Allah!

263
00:23:02,758 --> 00:23:04,186
Are you in love with Alaeddin?

264
00:23:07,029 --> 00:23:07,959
I'm asking you.

265
00:23:08,926 --> 00:23:10,739
I gave you a duty, but...

266
00:23:11,439 --> 00:23:12,496
Mother, what are you saying?

267
00:23:13,229 --> 00:23:14,382
You heard me.

268
00:23:17,116 --> 00:23:18,728
If I loved Alaeddin...

269
00:23:19,787 --> 00:23:21,020
would I tell you what I heard?

270
00:23:23,053 --> 00:23:25,194
Would I do such a thing?
Don't you know me, Mother?

271
00:23:26,727 --> 00:23:27,400
How would I know?

272
00:23:29,067 --> 00:23:30,201
It's love.

273
00:23:31,468 --> 00:23:33,626
One cannot know.

274
00:23:35,093 --> 00:23:36,751
Right? Gonca.

275
00:23:39,451 --> 00:23:42,309
You've defended the Kayıs many times.

276
00:23:43,209 --> 00:23:45,355
When Alaeddin was arrested,
you stood in your brother's way.

277
00:23:46,655 --> 00:23:47,313
Mother.

278
00:23:48,480 --> 00:23:50,827
I always said what
I believed to be right.

279
00:23:52,639 --> 00:23:54,050
What does this have
to do with Alaeddin?

280
00:23:56,434 --> 00:23:58,473
Don't disappoint me, Gonca.

281
00:24:02,455 --> 00:24:04,322
If you love Alaeddin...

282
00:24:05,722 --> 00:24:07,457
this will only burden you,
my daughter.

283
00:24:11,657 --> 00:24:12,590
You can go now.

284
00:24:16,921 --> 00:24:17,747
Don't forget.

285
00:24:22,108 --> 00:24:25,155
Alaeddin is only your duty.

286
00:24:37,314 --> 00:24:38,161
Fitnat.

287
00:24:39,991 --> 00:24:41,218
Tell Gülce...

288
00:24:42,459 --> 00:24:45,868
she will watch Gonca's every move
and inform me.

289
00:24:46,695 --> 00:24:48,953
- Do you understand?
- I understand, Saadet Hatun.

290
00:24:55,429 --> 00:24:57,172
Oh, Gonca.

291
00:24:59,090 --> 00:25:03,060
Your eyes and your heart differ,
my daughter.

292
00:25:04,820 --> 00:25:09,490
How did Mehmet Bey save you
in the raid? He is very brave.

293
00:25:09,810 --> 00:25:11,710
He values you obviously.

294
00:25:12,340 --> 00:25:16,720
What was Orhan Bey doing then?
He was busy saving Aysima.

295
00:25:18,160 --> 00:25:21,540
Have you really forgiven him?

296
00:25:21,840 --> 00:25:22,610
No.

297
00:25:24,400 --> 00:25:27,650
I haven't forgiven him,
I can't forgive him.

298
00:25:29,650 --> 00:25:31,650
I really want to forgive him.

299
00:25:33,390 --> 00:25:35,840
But that picture doesn't leave my mind.

300
00:25:46,480 --> 00:25:48,080
Have a good day, Holofira.

301
00:25:48,820 --> 00:25:53,120
You said you didn't want it, but I thought
you'd change your mind on seeing the horse.

302
00:26:02,270 --> 00:26:06,590
You are very thoughful.
It seems to be a thoroughbred horse

303
00:26:07,310 --> 00:26:08,590
Will you accept it?

304
00:26:13,390 --> 00:26:15,630
I probably behaved brash yesterday.

305
00:26:16,290 --> 00:26:19,740
I owe you my life and I couldn't thank you.

306
00:26:21,360 --> 00:26:25,180
If you accept the horse,
that will be your thanks.

307
00:26:31,220 --> 00:26:33,250
Refusing would be rude of me.

308
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:35,250
Thank you.

309
00:26:45,980 --> 00:26:47,870
You made me very happy, Holofira.

310
00:26:48,960 --> 00:26:53,280
You should know, seeing you
like this makes me feel better.

311
00:26:56,100 --> 00:26:57,440
Always smile.

312
00:26:58,590 --> 00:26:59,440
Thank you.

313
00:27:01,440 --> 00:27:02,780
I will go now.

314
00:27:08,130 --> 00:27:11,380
Holofira. What have you done?

315
00:27:13,890 --> 00:27:18,140
When my brother hears about this,
all Hell will break loose.

316
00:27:25,040 --> 00:27:26,960
Where are the Alps, Gökmen?

317
00:27:28,960 --> 00:27:31,680
Didn't I tell you that this tent
won't be left unguarded?

318
00:27:31,680 --> 00:27:33,470
- My Prince...
- Be quiet!

319
00:27:33,470 --> 00:27:35,220
Be quiet!

320
00:27:45,330 --> 00:27:47,020
Veysel!

321
00:27:49,920 --> 00:27:52,130
Gather your Alps quickly, Gökmen.

322
00:27:52,930 --> 00:27:54,130
Quickly!

323
00:27:58,290 --> 00:28:00,210
Alps!

324
00:28:08,820 --> 00:28:09,700
Bala Hatun.

325
00:28:10,610 --> 00:28:14,240
What is the reason we sent
Hasan Alp after that cart?

326
00:28:15,140 --> 00:28:19,200
The cart left the market
in a hurry.

327
00:28:19,650 --> 00:28:23,890
Clearly something is up.
They shouldn't leave the cart.

328
00:28:24,400 --> 00:28:26,940
They should find out who is inside.

329
00:28:27,360 --> 00:28:29,250
Our concern now is Alaeddin.

330
00:28:30,216 --> 00:28:31,047
Alright.

331
00:28:37,040 --> 00:28:41,810
My Bey, there are traces up to the water,
then they disappear. They are unclear.

332
00:28:43,810 --> 00:28:48,050
My Sultan, there's no trace. It's as if
they put on wings and flew away.

333
00:28:48,220 --> 00:28:50,530
We lost that baseborn dog!

334
00:28:51,630 --> 00:28:55,710
Who knows where he'll hide
and when he'll attack!

335
00:28:55,840 --> 00:28:57,540
This is because of you, Yakup Bey!

336
00:28:58,850 --> 00:29:02,930
You raided the Inn. You let
those who harmed us escape.

337
00:29:03,040 --> 00:29:05,280
They said that Osman was
the one who hurt my daughter.

338
00:29:05,630 --> 00:29:08,860
What should I have done?
My daughter's life was at risk.

339
00:29:09,440 --> 00:29:11,260
I wasn't going to just sit in my tent.

340
00:29:11,520 --> 00:29:16,210
Whoever said so is more of a
dog than those that escaped!

341
00:29:18,740 --> 00:29:20,820
Now we will return to the border market.

342
00:29:20,900 --> 00:29:26,210
If we trusted your words and came,
we don't trust you enough to let you go.

343
00:29:27,920 --> 00:29:29,940
You will face Veysel.

344
00:29:30,380 --> 00:29:33,580
We will see who's a traitor and who isn't.

345
00:29:35,180 --> 00:29:38,140
Let's go, Yakup Bey.
Let's definitely go.

346
00:29:40,740 --> 00:29:46,060
But if you fall into negligence and one of
the Mongols hurt someone in my family...

347
00:29:46,350 --> 00:29:48,060
you will pay dearly for this.

348
00:29:48,770 --> 00:29:50,060
Just so you know.

349
00:29:51,980 --> 00:29:55,180
You think about the answer you'll give first.

350
00:29:55,570 --> 00:29:57,390
Then hold us accountable.

351
00:30:00,750 --> 00:30:01,680
Come on.

352
00:30:04,740 --> 00:30:08,120
You can't even hold one man.

353
00:30:12,540 --> 00:30:13,730
And you?

354
00:30:16,420 --> 00:30:20,690
The man runs away in front of your
eyes you and you don't even realise.

355
00:30:28,560 --> 00:30:32,140
Gökmen, you embarrassed me.

356
00:30:32,590 --> 00:30:34,690
It's time for you to fix your mistake.

357
00:30:35,060 --> 00:30:38,560
- Don't come back until you find that man.
- As you command, my Prince.

358
00:30:40,880 --> 00:30:43,540
You will be punished for this failure.

359
00:30:44,060 --> 00:30:45,540
Get out of my sight now.

360
00:30:46,180 --> 00:30:48,500
- Get lost!
- Alps! Let's go!

361
00:30:55,740 --> 00:30:57,100
What happened, Mehmet?

362
00:30:58,830 --> 00:31:02,000
What is this state of the Alps, brother?

363
00:31:06,880 --> 00:31:07,440
Or...

364
00:31:08,130 --> 00:31:11,150
They took Veysel, Osman's Alp.

365
00:31:11,630 --> 00:31:14,530
How did they do this with all
these Alps around, Mehmet?

366
00:31:18,220 --> 00:31:19,260
Or was it Bala?

367
00:31:20,690 --> 00:31:21,260
No.

368
00:31:23,870 --> 00:31:25,870
We took precautions for the Kayı Alps.

369
00:31:26,900 --> 00:31:28,880
Gülce is watching Bala Hatun,
she couldn't do this.

370
00:31:32,580 --> 00:31:35,440
It's my fault, mother.

371
00:31:36,030 --> 00:31:37,680
I couldn't place strict measures.

372
00:31:39,090 --> 00:31:42,000
But I will find that dog wherever he goes.

373
00:31:43,240 --> 00:31:48,360
Maybe that Veysel is a traitor
as Alaeddin Bey said?

374
00:31:49,330 --> 00:31:54,090
Of course, he ran away when he
realised we'd find out about him.

375
00:31:55,120 --> 00:31:56,780
- Gonca!
- Gonca!

376
00:32:32,830 --> 00:32:36,140
Stop, driver! I said stop!

377
00:32:45,390 --> 00:32:47,860
Alps, be careful.

378
00:32:54,780 --> 00:32:55,810
You dog!

379
00:32:58,100 --> 00:32:59,360
Where will you run to?

380
00:33:04,770 --> 00:33:05,570
Keep going.

381
00:33:10,860 --> 00:33:15,370
You foolish Turks, you will never beat us.
We'll always find a way out.

382
00:33:16,160 --> 00:33:17,920
We will start, Lord Vasilis.

383
00:33:23,490 --> 00:33:25,420
Alps!

384
00:33:42,220 --> 00:33:45,210
The cloths were loaded onto the cart.
They're waiting for us, Lord Vasilis.

385
00:33:45,240 --> 00:33:46,990
You'll get on the cart quickly.

386
00:34:01,100 --> 00:34:02,260
Vasilis.

387
00:34:04,820 --> 00:34:05,870
My friend.

388
00:34:11,420 --> 00:34:12,909
I knew you wouldn't leave me.

389
00:34:18,380 --> 00:34:22,110
I would burn all the border lands
and take you from there.

390
00:34:22,340 --> 00:34:24,530
I know you would, Master Gera.

391
00:34:25,469 --> 00:34:29,081
And I would have burned myself
for the cause if you asked...

392
00:34:29,281 --> 00:34:30,434
Never.

393
00:34:31,679 --> 00:34:33,580
I would never sacrifice you.

394
00:34:35,989 --> 00:34:37,620
Your absence will make them crazy.

395
00:34:37,620 --> 00:34:40,230
Osman and Yakup will vent
their anger on each other.

396
00:34:42,080 --> 00:34:43,760
I already lit the fire between them.

397
00:34:44,760 --> 00:34:48,120
Yakup arrested Alaeddin and Bayındır
thanks to the strife I caused.

398
00:34:48,310 --> 00:34:51,070
He will detain them and
never release them.

399
00:34:51,070 --> 00:34:53,560
The old wolf will keep
them in place of you.

400
00:34:54,040 --> 00:34:56,360
I'm starting to get curious
about my next task from now.

401
00:34:57,790 --> 00:35:02,050
Osman will not stop before he proves
you are a traitor and saves his son.

402
00:35:02,610 --> 00:35:03,910
He won't stop following you.

403
00:35:04,700 --> 00:35:08,330
Your new task is to never get caught.

404
00:35:09,200 --> 00:35:11,850
Hide in a safe place and
wait for news from me.

405
00:35:12,420 --> 00:35:13,760
What about you, Master Gera?

406
00:35:14,860 --> 00:35:15,760
What's on your mind?

407
00:35:17,920 --> 00:35:19,060
I am a trader.

408
00:35:25,420 --> 00:35:26,200
Master Gera.

409
00:35:27,160 --> 00:35:29,220
Karacelasun is returning with his soldiers.

410
00:35:30,400 --> 00:35:32,800
- Osman and Yakup are...
- Alive!

411
00:35:36,370 --> 00:35:37,750
That big-headed Mongol!

412
00:35:41,060 --> 00:35:44,310
If it was possible to defeat without
tricks, we would have done it.

413
00:35:44,590 --> 00:35:46,050
The Mongols will learn this too!

414
00:35:47,610 --> 00:35:50,300
Let's go and meet the Mongols before Yakup.

415
00:35:51,090 --> 00:35:53,900
Let's explain to him why he couldn't kill him.

416
00:35:57,070 --> 00:35:58,010
Vasilis.

417
00:35:59,080 --> 00:36:00,300
Don't get caught.

418
00:36:01,610 --> 00:36:02,630
Wait for news from me.

419
00:36:04,580 --> 00:36:05,220
Come on.

420
00:36:06,270 --> 00:36:06,930
Let's go.

421
00:36:14,730 --> 00:36:18,310
Sultan Yakup is coming.
Osman Bey is coming.

422
00:36:23,050 --> 00:36:24,080
Osman?

423
00:36:25,740 --> 00:36:27,390
Why is he still alive now, mother?

424
00:36:27,670 --> 00:36:30,890
Your father must know something.
Don't question him, Mehmet.

425
00:36:31,750 --> 00:36:34,510
Worry about your own mistake.

426
00:36:41,110 --> 00:36:42,510
Praise be to Allah.

427
00:36:55,450 --> 00:36:56,600
Peace be upon you.

428
00:36:57,180 --> 00:37:00,570
- Peace be upon you.
- Peace be upon you.

429
00:37:02,250 --> 00:37:06,170
It seems Yakup Bey wasn't the only
one who believed the slander.

430
00:37:07,590 --> 00:37:09,830
But all the people believed this slander.

431
00:37:14,210 --> 00:37:19,090
While we were about to defeat that dog that
raided the market and caused us pain...

432
00:37:21,880 --> 00:37:24,170
Yakup Bey came and
let him escape.

433
00:37:25,700 --> 00:37:27,450
Now bring that dog who slandered me.

434
00:37:29,350 --> 00:37:30,530
Bring Veysel!

435
00:37:36,880 --> 00:37:38,150
Veysel escaped, my Bey.

436
00:37:58,250 --> 00:38:03,210
Did you do this so that he doesn't
speak the truth, Osman?

437
00:38:03,960 --> 00:38:05,490
Did you smuggle Veysel?

438
00:38:05,960 --> 00:38:08,370
You stand in front of me
with the word of a dog...

439
00:38:11,350 --> 00:38:14,190
we fight with you, back to back,
because you are one of us...

440
00:38:15,270 --> 00:38:18,140
and now you're trying to hold
us accountable for your failure.

441
00:38:18,770 --> 00:38:20,670
Watch your words, Osman Bey.

442
00:38:22,770 --> 00:38:24,620
Watch it so you can live long.

443
00:38:25,850 --> 00:38:28,590
Likewise, Yakup Bey.

444
00:38:29,490 --> 00:38:31,800
Let there be an to your slanders.

445
00:38:37,330 --> 00:38:39,530
You keep saying it's slander but...

446
00:38:40,550 --> 00:38:42,640
Bala Hatun has been in the
market for a long time.

447
00:38:43,880 --> 00:38:50,090
She says she wants Alaeddin, but it seems
there were other people she wanted.

448
00:38:50,740 --> 00:38:53,590
If you detain my son and
accuse me at the same time...

449
00:38:53,810 --> 00:38:56,960
it changes everything,
white becomes red, Saadet Hatun.

450
00:39:00,660 --> 00:39:01,280
Bala.

451
00:39:04,490 --> 00:39:05,780
Is Alaeddin a prisoner in your hands?

452
00:39:06,220 --> 00:39:11,370
I hold the whole world captive until the
matter becomes clear, if necessary.

453
00:39:12,340 --> 00:39:14,410
Who is Alaeddin, Osman Bey?

454
00:39:14,660 --> 00:39:17,850
I will make the world Hell for the
one who imprisons Alaeddin.

455
00:39:20,360 --> 00:39:21,490
Don't hesitate.

456
00:39:23,010 --> 00:39:24,390
Whoever hesitates hurts me.

457
00:39:26,130 --> 00:39:27,770
Go first, Mehmet Bey.

458
00:39:34,590 --> 00:39:35,390
Alps!

459
00:39:39,530 --> 00:39:41,670
Close all entrances and
exits to the market.

460
00:39:43,960 --> 00:39:45,570
Veysel is one of the Crusaders.

461
00:39:46,500 --> 00:39:48,090
Clearly there is a traitor inside.

462
00:39:48,770 --> 00:39:50,450
They allowed him to escape.

463
00:39:51,050 --> 00:39:54,130
There can be no traitor on my land.

464
00:39:54,840 --> 00:39:58,500
Do you want the truth or
do you want problems?

465
00:40:20,770 --> 00:40:22,250
They believed in victory.

466
00:40:23,860 --> 00:40:25,590
They fell into ambushes.

467
00:40:26,260 --> 00:40:29,820
We ripped the courage
out of their hearts.

468
00:40:31,580 --> 00:40:34,360
And now we will take their lives.

469
00:40:54,290 --> 00:40:55,460
I told you.

470
00:40:58,520 --> 00:41:01,900
If you had listened to me,
you wouldn't have been wounded.

471
00:41:06,890 --> 00:41:09,130
Crusader.

472
00:41:12,610 --> 00:41:15,590
We live to fight.

473
00:41:17,180 --> 00:41:19,280
Our wounds are our path.

474
00:41:20,750 --> 00:41:22,800
Our path is known, Mongols.

475
00:41:23,940 --> 00:41:25,850
Yakup captured Osman's son.

476
00:41:27,850 --> 00:41:29,080
My game is ready.

477
00:41:29,810 --> 00:41:30,530
Think.

478
00:41:31,700 --> 00:41:36,090
So far, we have set Yakup upon Osman.

479
00:41:36,550 --> 00:41:38,070
But what did Osman do?

480
00:41:39,130 --> 00:41:41,910
He was not defeated by his pride.
He assumed humility.

481
00:41:43,650 --> 00:41:45,350
He did not fight Yakup.

482
00:41:46,140 --> 00:41:48,220
Yakup is not like Osman.

483
00:41:48,790 --> 00:41:49,640
Not at all.

484
00:41:49,970 --> 00:41:53,170
He is arrogant and ambitious.

485
00:41:53,970 --> 00:41:56,490
When Osman walks towards Yakup...

486
00:41:56,940 --> 00:42:01,310
Yakup will be defeated by his
pride, he will not assume humility.

487
00:42:01,780 --> 00:42:04,530
He will fall for the game and enter into war.

488
00:42:11,450 --> 00:42:12,510
Karacelasun.

489
00:42:15,250 --> 00:42:18,120
Osman's son, Alaeddin...

490
00:42:19,860 --> 00:42:22,930
His intelligent and most valuable one.

491
00:42:24,140 --> 00:42:25,440
We will kill him.

492
00:42:31,990 --> 00:42:34,360
We will put the blame on Yakup.

493
00:42:37,730 --> 00:42:39,340
I like your game, Crusader.

494
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:43,610
You do that and I'll do my part.

495
00:42:48,890 --> 00:42:50,210
Great Mergen.

496
00:42:52,220 --> 00:42:53,560
Listen to Erlik Han.

497
00:43:13,850 --> 00:43:16,770
I hear Erlik Han.

498
00:43:42,370 --> 00:43:45,660
He sends them death.

499
00:44:36,770 --> 00:44:39,460
So, you're the traitor? Come on!

500
00:44:40,430 --> 00:44:41,300
Come here!

501
00:44:45,590 --> 00:44:46,210
Come on!

502
00:44:54,010 --> 00:44:54,660
Kneel!

503
00:44:55,980 --> 00:44:58,030
My Bey, this is the traitor.

504
00:45:04,330 --> 00:45:05,130
Dağhan Alp.

505
00:45:06,610 --> 00:45:07,660
Don't slander, Orhan.

506
00:45:07,940 --> 00:45:09,950
The one who infiltrated my palace...

507
00:45:10,340 --> 00:45:12,700
will he hesitate to enter your market,
Mehmet?

508
00:45:25,540 --> 00:45:26,900
Until Veysel is found...

509
00:45:28,450 --> 00:45:30,090
this dog will continue to breathe.

510
00:45:31,370 --> 00:45:34,490
They bring the poison of the Mongols
with the hands of the Crusaders.

511
00:45:36,490 --> 00:45:38,070
It is clear that they have allied.

512
00:45:39,520 --> 00:45:41,090
We will find out who they are.

513
00:45:42,360 --> 00:45:43,120
That's why...

514
00:45:44,540 --> 00:45:46,250
this dog will live until then.

515
00:45:50,000 --> 00:45:51,120
Look at me.

516
00:45:53,490 --> 00:45:55,000
You will release Alaeddin.

517
00:45:55,770 --> 00:45:59,700
I will find that Veysel and I will bring
him and throw him before your eyes.

518
00:46:01,130 --> 00:46:02,170
Let it be my promise.

519
00:46:04,300 --> 00:46:05,180
Kanyumaz.

520
00:46:10,880 --> 00:46:12,290
Alaeddin is alive.

521
00:46:12,880 --> 00:46:13,930
He is fine.

522
00:46:14,340 --> 00:46:15,910
Until Veysel is found...

523
00:46:16,850 --> 00:46:18,650
he will be my guest.

524
00:46:21,500 --> 00:46:22,670
Yakup Bey.

525
00:46:24,640 --> 00:46:25,680
Look.

526
00:46:26,630 --> 00:46:29,230
I am striving to improve the situation.

527
00:46:30,850 --> 00:46:31,960
But you...

528
00:46:32,930 --> 00:46:34,530
you are ruining everything.

529
00:46:36,510 --> 00:46:38,270
While I'm trying not to spill blood...

530
00:46:39,480 --> 00:46:41,630
you are forcing the blood to be spilled.

531
00:46:43,000 --> 00:46:44,500
If my son is not released...

532
00:46:45,370 --> 00:46:47,400
I will be the first to shed blood, enough!

533
00:46:47,820 --> 00:46:50,480
Perhaps your blood will be spilled first, Bala.

534
00:47:05,440 --> 00:47:07,010
- Mother.
- Son?

535
00:47:07,520 --> 00:47:08,550
Father.

536
00:47:09,230 --> 00:47:10,270
Alaeddin.

537
00:47:10,640 --> 00:47:11,740
Brother.

538
00:47:13,780 --> 00:47:15,170
Veysel's betrayal is clear.

539
00:47:16,130 --> 00:47:17,150
He will be found.

540
00:47:18,610 --> 00:47:19,790
We have no fear.

541
00:47:21,610 --> 00:47:23,370
Since Yakup Bey has doubts...

542
00:47:24,480 --> 00:47:25,950
and wants leverage...

543
00:47:27,510 --> 00:47:29,530
I have no objection in being his guest,
my Bey.

544
00:47:34,270 --> 00:47:35,410
No. No.

545
00:47:37,870 --> 00:47:38,950
Mother.

546
00:47:39,730 --> 00:47:40,820
There's no problem.

547
00:47:42,020 --> 00:47:43,590
Yakup Bey will host me well.

548
00:47:46,190 --> 00:47:47,290
Don't be upset.

549
00:47:56,340 --> 00:47:57,850
We found one traitor...

550
00:47:59,060 --> 00:48:00,350
we will find the other one too.

551
00:48:00,970 --> 00:48:03,600
But, Yakup Bey, until then...

552
00:48:04,190 --> 00:48:06,230
if a hair on my son's head is hurt...

553
00:48:07,000 --> 00:48:08,110
this market...

554
00:48:08,470 --> 00:48:10,780
and this tent, I will bring it down
over your head, just so you know.

555
00:48:13,710 --> 00:48:15,120
For your own betterment...

556
00:48:16,760 --> 00:48:19,460
I'll assume I didn't hear these words,
Osman Bey.

557
00:48:23,240 --> 00:48:24,660
You have two days.

558
00:48:25,950 --> 00:48:27,260
Bring Veysel...

559
00:48:27,960 --> 00:48:29,210
and take Alaeddin.

560
00:48:30,930 --> 00:48:32,480
Otherwise this is hosting...

561
00:48:33,490 --> 00:48:35,820
will turn into a difficult captivity.

562
00:48:39,850 --> 00:48:41,240
When the truth comes out...

563
00:48:42,770 --> 00:48:45,120
how will you pay for this slander?

564
00:48:46,570 --> 00:48:48,880
There are many prices to be paid,
Osman Bey.

565
00:48:52,660 --> 00:48:53,750
Two days.

566
00:48:58,450 --> 00:48:59,560
Go on.

567
00:49:00,060 --> 00:49:01,250
Have a safe journey.

568
00:49:14,300 --> 00:49:15,340
Alps!

569
00:49:20,810 --> 00:49:21,810
Bala Hatun.

570
00:49:22,150 --> 00:49:24,390
Allow me to come with you.

571
00:49:25,610 --> 00:49:26,620
Come, my daughter, come.

572
00:49:30,590 --> 00:49:31,640
Brother.

573
00:49:32,270 --> 00:49:33,580
Holofira is going home.

574
00:49:34,240 --> 00:49:35,690
She left with her new horse a while ago.

575
00:49:37,780 --> 00:49:38,930
What horse, sister?

576
00:49:39,580 --> 00:49:40,640
What are you saying?

577
00:49:40,880 --> 00:49:42,790
Mehmet Bey gifted her a horse.

578
00:49:43,420 --> 00:49:44,570
And Holofira accepted it.

579
00:49:45,380 --> 00:49:46,920
I never expected her to accept it.

580
00:49:48,590 --> 00:49:49,610
So she accepted it?

581
00:49:50,620 --> 00:49:51,780
So she accepted it?

582
00:49:53,040 --> 00:49:54,700
I shouldn't have said this.

583
00:49:55,430 --> 00:49:56,910
I hope from Allah that this tongue of mine...

584
00:49:58,420 --> 00:49:59,510
Holofira.

585
00:50:15,350 --> 00:50:18,220
The dark spirits will drag them to death.

586
00:50:19,020 --> 00:50:20,910
Their end will come soon.

587
00:50:25,910 --> 00:50:27,090
My soldiers!

588
00:50:28,740 --> 00:50:29,870
My revenge...

589
00:50:30,630 --> 00:50:31,650
will become a legend...

590
00:50:32,340 --> 00:50:34,170
and reach the other world.

591
00:50:35,930 --> 00:50:36,990
But...

592
00:50:37,750 --> 00:50:39,740
first, we need soldiers for this.

593
00:50:41,700 --> 00:50:42,770
We...

594
00:50:43,210 --> 00:50:45,510
are enough for them,
Commander Karacelasun.

595
00:50:47,130 --> 00:50:49,440
No. No.

596
00:50:52,290 --> 00:50:53,870
The more we are...

597
00:50:54,910 --> 00:50:56,450
The more we are...

598
00:50:56,910 --> 00:50:58,760
the less our blood will be spilled.

599
00:51:01,170 --> 00:51:02,350
Every drop...

600
00:51:03,170 --> 00:51:04,730
of my soldiers' blood...

601
00:51:06,410 --> 00:51:07,950
is a gift from Erlik Han.

602
00:51:14,920 --> 00:51:16,310
We will live...

603
00:51:16,850 --> 00:51:17,960
and they will die!

604
00:51:31,500 --> 00:51:32,540
Mergen.

605
00:51:34,460 --> 00:51:36,510
Tomorrow you will quickly go to Tabriz.

606
00:51:37,250 --> 00:51:40,550
Soldiers there who are waiting to die...

607
00:51:40,740 --> 00:51:42,000
you'll bring them with you.

608
00:51:42,337 --> 00:51:44,296
- As you command, Commander Karacelasun.
- Go on.

609
00:51:55,670 --> 00:51:57,080
When the soldiers come...

610
00:51:57,790 --> 00:52:01,930
I will feed Osman's head to the dogs.

611
00:52:06,280 --> 00:52:07,570
In Sha Allah.
(If Allah permits)

612
00:52:09,510 --> 00:52:10,730
- In Sha Allah.
- In Sha Allah.

613
00:52:12,290 --> 00:52:13,890
In Sha Allah, Karacelasun.

614
00:52:14,170 --> 00:52:16,770
Well then, trader Ayhan Ağa...

615
00:52:17,220 --> 00:52:18,500
should go to the border market.

616
00:52:19,100 --> 00:52:23,120
Let us talk a little with Yakup Bey.

617
00:52:24,040 --> 00:52:25,890
While we talk...

618
00:52:26,590 --> 00:52:33,420
let your heroes strike the neck of Osman's
son Alaeddin whose mind is valuable.

619
00:52:34,290 --> 00:52:36,240
Then what will Osman Bey do?

620
00:52:37,750 --> 00:52:39,400
He will have lost his son.

621
00:52:40,830 --> 00:52:42,780
He will take revenge...

622
00:52:44,100 --> 00:52:45,900
for his valuable Alaeddin Bey.

623
00:52:46,790 --> 00:52:48,350
In order to avenge his son...

624
00:52:48,810 --> 00:52:50,600
he will attack Yakup Bey.

625
00:52:51,990 --> 00:52:54,140
Then, Alaeddin's...

626
00:52:54,710 --> 00:52:56,650
head full of knowledge...

627
00:52:57,830 --> 00:53:01,650
I will gift it to your soldiers.

628
00:53:02,370 --> 00:53:05,050
I make things easier for your soldiers.

629
00:53:07,420 --> 00:53:08,470
Victory is one...

630
00:53:09,340 --> 00:53:11,140
and the enemy is one, Crusader.

631
00:53:32,320 --> 00:53:33,340
We'll talk.

632
00:53:37,410 --> 00:53:38,530
Come on.

633
00:54:06,940 --> 00:54:08,000
What do you want?

634
00:54:13,930 --> 00:54:15,410
You liked the gift very much,
didn't you?

635
00:54:16,140 --> 00:54:18,460
It seems word spreads very fast
in these border lands.

636
00:54:18,750 --> 00:54:20,750
Holofira, how could you...

637
00:54:21,270 --> 00:54:23,040
how could you accept Mehmet's gift?

638
00:54:23,240 --> 00:54:24,890
Do you expect me to answer to you?

639
00:54:25,990 --> 00:54:27,270
Who are you, Orhan?

640
00:54:28,030 --> 00:54:29,250
Who are you to me?

641
00:54:30,960 --> 00:54:32,790
- I am your...
- What are you to me?

642
00:54:35,230 --> 00:54:36,640
Who are you to me, Orhan?

643
00:54:39,760 --> 00:54:42,060
You can't say it, but I'll say it.

644
00:54:43,430 --> 00:54:45,300
You are no one to me.

645
00:54:49,610 --> 00:54:50,930
You cannot interfere in my matters.

646
00:54:51,620 --> 00:54:54,030
If you want to interfere so much,
go and interfere with your sister Fatma.

647
00:54:55,120 --> 00:54:56,200
Or in fact...

648
00:54:56,880 --> 00:54:59,210
what was her name? Aysima...

649
00:55:01,690 --> 00:55:03,630
go and interfere in her matters
if you so badly want to.

650
00:55:03,770 --> 00:55:06,280
In any case, she's inside the palace
next to your mother, isn't it?

651
00:55:06,420 --> 00:55:08,170
That gift you took from Mehmet...

652
00:55:09,630 --> 00:55:10,860
you'll give it back, Holofira.

653
00:55:12,040 --> 00:55:13,630
Maybe she made you sweetmeat again.

654
00:55:14,390 --> 00:55:15,550
You liked it very much.

655
00:55:17,240 --> 00:55:18,240
Go and eat it.

656
00:55:22,680 --> 00:55:23,790
Aysima...

657
00:55:24,580 --> 00:55:26,040
is no one to me.

658
00:55:29,130 --> 00:55:30,710
Is that why you saved her life?

659
00:55:59,810 --> 00:56:00,910
So...

660
00:56:01,370 --> 00:56:03,170
the freedom of my prince...

661
00:56:03,730 --> 00:56:05,280
depends on what you say, is it?

662
00:56:12,050 --> 00:56:14,090
Look at me,
you will speak.

663
00:56:14,820 --> 00:56:16,010
You will speak.

664
00:56:20,950 --> 00:56:22,440
- Wait.
- That's more like it.

665
00:56:23,340 --> 00:56:24,350
Veysel...

666
00:56:26,630 --> 00:56:27,740
his real name...

667
00:56:29,910 --> 00:56:31,740
is Vasilis.

668
00:56:36,080 --> 00:56:38,330
He is above us.

669
00:56:39,040 --> 00:56:40,190
Keep talking, go on.

670
00:56:40,750 --> 00:56:41,910
I will speak because...

671
00:56:43,990 --> 00:56:45,020
we...

672
00:56:47,600 --> 00:56:48,850
will kill all of you.

673
00:56:49,820 --> 00:56:51,490
What is this disgrace?

674
00:56:52,220 --> 00:56:53,250
Mehmet?

675
00:56:53,700 --> 00:56:55,290
You lost the man in your hand.

676
00:56:56,710 --> 00:56:57,980
And the Alp under your command...

677
00:56:58,440 --> 00:56:59,500
turns out a traitor.

678
00:57:02,300 --> 00:57:04,240
While everything is mixed up...

679
00:57:05,000 --> 00:57:06,110
don't pressure Mehmet.

680
00:57:09,470 --> 00:57:10,770
Should it have been...

681
00:57:11,960 --> 00:57:14,160
Osman's Alps who found the tracks, Hatun?

682
00:57:20,610 --> 00:57:22,210
Even the traitor among us...

683
00:57:23,090 --> 00:57:24,300
should they have discovered it?

684
00:57:27,260 --> 00:57:28,510
And while we say that our son...

685
00:57:29,060 --> 00:57:30,210
is brave...

686
00:57:31,390 --> 00:57:32,390
and crafty...

687
00:57:32,600 --> 00:57:34,500
There will never be such weakness again.

688
00:57:34,820 --> 00:57:36,000
Let there not be, Mehmet.

689
00:57:36,570 --> 00:57:37,740
Let there not be.

690
00:57:39,290 --> 00:57:41,150
I will not accept mistakes anymore.

691
00:57:44,230 --> 00:57:46,450
Keep the Alps alert.

692
00:57:47,180 --> 00:57:52,210
And let's be ready when Cerkutay brings
information from Osman's palace.

693
00:57:52,430 --> 00:57:54,500
As you command, my Bey.

694
00:58:01,220 --> 00:58:03,820
- May I come in, my Sultan?
- Come in.

695
00:58:08,533 --> 00:58:11,699
My Sultan, Ayhan Ağa has come.
He would like to see you.

696
00:58:13,780 --> 00:58:14,840
Let him wait.

697
00:58:28,540 --> 00:58:30,250
My prince is coming.

698
00:58:34,070 --> 00:58:38,770
My brother is a prisoner there, couldn't
you make this traitor is speak, valiants?

699
00:58:39,070 --> 00:58:39,838
My prince.

700
00:58:40,617 --> 00:58:42,688
Baysungur said to cut his tongue...

701
00:58:43,112 --> 00:58:45,712
we didn't want to lose hope,
we waited for you.

702
00:58:47,670 --> 00:58:50,590
You need not lose hope
and cut his tongue.

703
00:58:53,620 --> 00:58:56,219
While there are many places
which can be cut...

704
00:58:58,411 --> 00:58:59,361
Aykurt.

705
00:59:05,830 --> 00:59:12,310
This man is a warrior. He's
not afraid of beatings or death.

706
00:59:15,540 --> 00:59:17,050
But...

707
00:59:25,140 --> 00:59:27,130
But which way you die matters.

708
00:59:29,600 --> 00:59:31,810
My brother taught me.

709
00:59:32,570 --> 00:59:38,760
If I cut his neck from here, the blood
will flow fast and he will die quickly.

710
00:59:39,820 --> 00:59:41,800
But that doesn't work for me.

711
00:59:44,160 --> 00:59:45,680
But if I cut from here...

712
00:59:46,505 --> 00:59:49,562
the blood will flow from his mouth and nose...

713
00:59:49,839 --> 00:59:51,197
and in his own blood...

714
00:59:55,849 --> 00:59:56,932
he will drown.

715
00:59:57,770 --> 01:00:01,280
As long as you don't speak, my
brother will remain captive there.

716
01:00:01,550 --> 01:00:03,112
If something happens to
him while he's there...

717
01:00:03,652 --> 01:00:05,266
I will cut you into pieces...

718
01:00:05,697 --> 01:00:07,396
and bury your pieces everywhere.

719
01:00:11,060 --> 01:00:11,922
Alps!

720
01:00:12,821 --> 01:00:14,924
Hang him from his feet and start cutting.

721
01:00:15,720 --> 01:00:19,480
Let his blood flow inside it so
our land does not get dirty.

722
01:00:19,550 --> 01:00:23,370
And if he speaks, tell me.

723
01:00:23,500 --> 01:00:24,970
Okay, my prince.

724
01:00:25,320 --> 01:00:28,610
Alps, let's hang this dog.

725
01:00:31,358 --> 01:00:34,290
It bothers me to leave Alaeddin
there like this, Osman.

726
01:00:35,110 --> 01:00:38,160
Bala is right, they can't be trusted.

727
01:00:38,460 --> 01:00:42,890
Don't worry, Yakup Bey can't do anything.

728
01:00:45,080 --> 01:00:47,810
He wouldn't dare do something like that.

729
01:00:51,730 --> 01:00:54,000
Let's go now...

730
01:00:54,640 --> 01:00:56,980
let's go and find this dog.

731
01:01:03,880 --> 01:01:06,930
- My Bey.
- Son, come.

732
01:01:07,910 --> 01:01:11,140
My Bey, how do you think
they got him out?

733
01:01:11,940 --> 01:01:15,030
The market can be easily infiltrated by cart.

734
01:01:16,390 --> 01:01:18,520
The Mongols have done the same.

735
01:01:18,840 --> 01:01:21,100
And then they can leave
with the cart too.

736
01:01:22,150 --> 01:01:24,890
When we were in the market,
a cart left in a hurry.

737
01:01:25,473 --> 01:01:26,655
I sent Hasan after it.

738
01:01:26,855 --> 01:01:29,810
If he's in the cart, we'll find him soon.

739
01:01:30,390 --> 01:01:33,670
Well thought, Bala.
Well thought.

740
01:01:34,880 --> 01:01:38,234
But we will never give
the enemy a chance.

741
01:01:39,305 --> 01:01:42,257
We will always go after the clues.

742
01:01:44,260 --> 01:01:49,980
They don't think about Alaeddin or Veysel.

743
01:01:52,263 --> 01:01:54,382
While we were happy because
Mongols were becoming Muslim...

744
01:01:54,923 --> 01:01:58,087
but one shaman appeared and
ruined everything.

745
01:01:59,160 --> 01:02:02,190
As if that wasn't enough, they
united with the Crusaders.

746
01:02:04,860 --> 01:02:11,070
If they unite, we will unite too.

747
01:02:13,560 --> 01:02:17,730
Tell me, who has taken Candar Bey's place?

748
01:02:18,190 --> 01:02:22,520
His son, Süleyman Bey. He was chosen
by majority vote in the council, my Bey.

749
01:02:24,480 --> 01:02:27,581
We went to these Beys and saved them...

750
01:02:29,453 --> 01:02:30,946
and we gained a great reputation.

751
01:02:32,940 --> 01:02:38,470
But we have not used this reputation yet.

752
01:02:41,665 --> 01:02:42,677
Now...

753
01:02:43,129 --> 01:02:44,779
send messengers to the Beys.

754
01:02:46,482 --> 01:02:49,379
The Beys we called for war, let them come.

755
01:02:49,700 --> 01:02:52,790
Let them come to our court
and sit at our table.

756
01:02:53,580 --> 01:02:57,930
Because we must unite as well.

757
01:02:59,770 --> 01:03:02,790
My Bey, what is your
goal with this move?

758
01:03:02,960 --> 01:03:06,310
We withdrew our pledge and
made our move.

759
01:03:06,900 --> 01:03:09,710
Now I am curious about their loyalty.

760
01:03:11,720 --> 01:03:13,632
When I say I will lead...

761
01:03:14,746 --> 01:03:19,750
I will see who will stand behind me
and who will stand against me.

762
01:03:23,410 --> 01:03:26,620
- May I come in, my Bey?
- Come in.

763
01:03:41,260 --> 01:03:44,194
GERMIYANOĞLU BORDER / BORDER MARKET

764
01:03:44,394 --> 01:03:47,160
Everything that befalls us
benefits Osman.

765
01:03:47,840 --> 01:03:49,950
He is always looking for our weaknesses.

766
01:03:51,280 --> 01:03:55,150
It's enough, mother, I'll solve this.

767
01:03:55,440 --> 01:03:57,200
Of course you will solve it.

768
01:03:57,950 --> 01:04:02,490
But first you will take care of Holofira.

769
01:04:06,370 --> 01:04:10,120
She is on my mind, mother.
I take hold of her slowly.

770
01:04:11,050 --> 01:04:15,280
She accepted the horse I gave her today.
Her temperament was very good.

771
01:04:16,100 --> 01:04:21,190
Don't go slowly, my lion.
It's time to hurry.

772
01:04:22,820 --> 01:04:25,730
Tell Holofira of your intention tomorrow.

773
01:04:27,170 --> 01:04:29,020
Tell her you want to marry her.

774
01:04:38,560 --> 01:04:40,540
As you wish, mother.

775
01:04:43,579 --> 01:04:44,592
My Sultan...

776
01:04:44,975 --> 01:04:46,930
I know, I'm disturbing you, but...

777
01:04:47,563 --> 01:04:50,524
the recent unfortunate events...

778
01:04:51,771 --> 01:04:53,128
you know about it.

779
01:04:54,350 --> 01:04:56,013
These things happen all the time.

780
01:04:57,317 --> 01:04:59,369
We didn't come to know the Mongols yesterday,
Ayhan Ağa.

781
01:04:59,830 --> 01:05:02,620
It certainly is

782
01:05:03,770 --> 01:05:04,832
But...

783
01:05:05,573 --> 01:05:07,980
the customers, the source of our blessing...

784
01:05:08,787 --> 01:05:11,537
they fear for their lives, my Sultan.

785
01:05:12,400 --> 01:05:18,730
They no longer come to the market, and
when they don't come, our profits decline.

786
01:05:19,160 --> 01:05:23,840
Well, you kept saying you're a good trader.

787
01:05:25,270 --> 01:05:29,450
If you didn't have a solution,
you wouldn't come to meet me.

788
01:05:32,510 --> 01:05:37,240
My Sultan, I don't have a solution.

789
01:05:38,880 --> 01:05:41,410
But I have great concerns.

790
01:05:47,990 --> 01:05:50,540
Tell me without stalling, Ayhan Ağa.

791
01:05:51,430 --> 01:05:53,130
The Mongols, my sultan.

792
01:05:54,080 --> 01:05:56,422
I mean, those murderers...

793
01:05:58,054 --> 01:06:01,951
these barbarians, if they
want to kill everyone...

794
01:06:02,810 --> 01:06:04,007
they would do it...

795
01:06:06,050 --> 01:06:07,042
with pleasure.

796
01:06:07,250 --> 01:06:10,025
They raid and they leave halfway.

797
01:06:10,412 --> 01:06:11,306
Then...

798
01:06:12,830 --> 01:06:14,535
I mean, the traitors...

799
01:06:15,080 --> 01:06:19,120
walk out of here freely.

800
01:06:22,100 --> 01:06:26,765
Now, my Sultan, these incidents break trust.

801
01:06:26,965 --> 01:06:28,683
- Trust...
- What does that mean, Ayhan Ağa?

802
01:06:29,810 --> 01:06:31,640
Are these all games?

803
01:06:37,480 --> 01:06:38,525
Mehmet Bey.

804
01:06:40,465 --> 01:06:42,472
I don't want to say, but...

805
01:06:43,010 --> 01:06:45,290
what I think is...

806
01:06:47,170 --> 01:06:52,427
one of they Beys amongst you...

807
01:06:54,309 --> 01:06:55,795
agrees with them.

808
01:07:00,180 --> 01:07:05,920
And creates a new market,
that's what I understand.

809
01:07:07,540 --> 01:07:09,570
What do you know, Ayhan Ağa?

810
01:07:45,540 --> 01:07:47,670
The time has come, my brothers.

811
01:07:49,259 --> 01:07:53,110
Alaeddin will die tonight, let's get started.

812
01:08:11,856 --> 01:08:14,880
My Bey, what Orhan Bey did worked.

813
01:08:15,090 --> 01:08:18,729
The dog told us about the place.
It is a place near the Karapınar region.

814
01:08:21,660 --> 01:08:24,470
My Bey, let me quickly go and get him.

815
01:08:24,859 --> 01:08:27,689
No, stop, son.

816
01:08:28,870 --> 01:08:30,200
We will wait.

817
01:08:32,859 --> 01:08:34,149
We will wait.

818
01:08:36,380 --> 01:08:41,479
My Bey, forgive me, but
I agree with the prince.

819
01:08:42,649 --> 01:08:45,840
If Hasan comes and tells us another place,
let's raid that place too.

820
01:08:46,920 --> 01:08:50,310
Our time is tight, and
we have no time to wait.

821
01:08:51,772 --> 01:08:53,750
My Bey must know something.

822
01:08:56,240 --> 01:09:00,029
Of course. Osman Bey would
like to be sure first.

823
01:09:01,979 --> 01:09:04,210
If the place the traitor told us...

824
01:09:04,410 --> 01:09:06,180
is different from the place Hasan tells us...

825
01:09:07,453 --> 01:09:08,975
one of them will be a trap.

826
01:09:14,057 --> 01:09:15,870
May I come in, my Bey?

827
01:09:17,912 --> 01:09:19,649
Come in.

828
01:09:21,609 --> 01:09:25,560
My Bey, I watched the cart up
to the Karapınar region.

829
01:09:25,910 --> 01:09:28,920
Some of them clashed with me
then the cart disappeared from sight.

830
01:09:29,450 --> 01:09:32,790
I saw him, my Bey.
Veysel was inside it.

831
01:09:36,890 --> 01:09:38,290
My Bey.

832
01:09:38,540 --> 01:09:42,109
The place Hasan tells us about
is the same as what the traitor said.

833
01:09:42,340 --> 01:09:43,689
Veysel is there, my Bey.

834
01:09:43,890 --> 01:09:45,240
Let's go and get him and come back.

835
01:09:45,550 --> 01:09:49,040
Didn't you say that Veysel has a
high position among the Crusaders?

836
01:09:49,319 --> 01:09:53,189
These people will not tell who their
superior is even when they're dying.

837
01:09:55,200 --> 01:09:57,590
They also cut off Hasan's path.

838
01:09:57,920 --> 01:10:01,030
They know very well that
we are after them.

839
01:10:04,237 --> 01:10:05,360
My Bey.

840
01:10:05,790 --> 01:10:09,200
Do you mean the traitor is
taking us into a trap?

841
01:10:09,410 --> 01:10:11,800
Exactly that, he is setting a trap for us.

842
01:10:11,930 --> 01:10:13,560
But don't forget, son...

843
01:10:13,790 --> 01:10:19,980
if we know where the trap is,
we'll be setting the real trap.

844
01:10:22,270 --> 01:10:24,870
Veysel sets a trap for us.

845
01:10:29,420 --> 01:10:32,200
We said Crusaders are cooperating
with the Mongols, my Bey.

846
01:10:32,680 --> 01:10:34,720
Will it be just be Veysel?

847
01:10:35,100 --> 01:10:38,260
Brother, is that dog Karacelasun also there?

848
01:10:40,020 --> 01:10:44,700
Everyone wants this, they want to destroy us.

849
01:10:45,902 --> 01:10:48,805
Let them come, whatever the outcome...

850
01:10:49,572 --> 01:10:51,170
we'll take Veysel.

851
01:10:51,370 --> 01:10:53,260
There will be many dogs.

852
01:10:53,510 --> 01:10:54,890
Get ready.

853
01:10:55,300 --> 01:10:57,050
As my Bey commands.

854
01:11:01,615 --> 01:11:03,800
We'll take that dog first...

855
01:11:04,680 --> 01:11:06,370
and then my brother.

856
01:11:08,210 --> 01:11:13,300
I won't differentiate between any of them.

857
01:11:15,282 --> 01:11:20,380
Bala, prepare the yard
while we make our move.

858
01:11:20,710 --> 01:11:23,510
When the Beys enter, they
will see our prestige.

859
01:11:24,400 --> 01:11:28,750
Don't worry, my Bey. When the
great Turk Beys enter the palace...

860
01:11:28,780 --> 01:11:30,410
they will see what prestige is.

861
01:11:31,000 --> 01:11:33,470
Thank you.

862
01:11:35,910 --> 01:11:37,010
Malhun.

863
01:11:37,640 --> 01:11:41,870
Go to the border market,
don't let them out of your sight.

864
01:11:42,280 --> 01:11:44,850
My eyes will be on Germiyan, my Bey.

865
01:11:45,130 --> 01:11:46,760
Thank you.

866
01:11:47,070 --> 01:11:52,870
We will make our move
and heads will fall.

867
01:11:55,390 --> 01:12:00,510
After that there will be war,
then there'll be weddings.

868
01:12:00,840 --> 01:12:03,820
- In Sha Allah.
- In Sha Allah.

869
01:12:03,970 --> 01:12:05,860
In Sha Allah, my Bey.

870
01:12:11,180 --> 01:12:14,950
In fact, I wanted to leave you hungry, but...

871
01:12:16,890 --> 01:12:18,900
I can't hurt you.

872
01:12:54,290 --> 01:12:56,460
There's a trap.

873
01:12:57,710 --> 01:13:02,570
Alaeddin.
Alps!

874
01:13:10,110 --> 01:13:14,000
Yakup Bey has ordered,
you will die tonight, Alaeddin.

875
01:13:14,280 --> 01:13:16,960
Only Allah knows this.

876
01:13:50,450 --> 01:13:52,000
Bala?

877
01:13:52,737 --> 01:13:53,613
Bala.

878
01:13:54,891 --> 01:13:56,956
Alaeddin...

879
01:13:57,468 --> 01:13:58,019
Bala.

880
01:13:58,219 --> 01:14:01,420
Sit down, are you okay?

881
01:14:04,160 --> 01:14:06,420
I have a bad feeling in my heart.

882
01:14:07,460 --> 01:14:08,550
Don't.

883
01:14:09,830 --> 01:14:13,760
We will stand strong, we will not give up.
Don't worry.

884
01:14:14,620 --> 01:14:17,480
I will save my son from their hands.

885
01:14:40,950 --> 01:14:41,860
Are you okay?

886
01:14:41,970 --> 01:14:45,260
- I'm fine. Are you?
- I'm fine, it's nothing.

887
01:14:46,540 --> 01:14:50,240
Since you doubt the
establishment of a market...

888
01:14:50,670 --> 01:14:55,410
tell me completely now,
what do you know?

889
01:14:55,610 --> 01:14:56,900
My Sultan...

890
01:14:57,930 --> 01:15:00,970
I don't want to bear anyone's guilt.

891
01:15:01,570 --> 01:15:04,230
- But...
- But what, Ayhan Ağa?

892
01:15:07,140 --> 01:15:09,120
If there was a market like you claim...

893
01:15:09,400 --> 01:15:13,310
everyone who sets a stall in that market
has declared war on us.

894
01:15:13,590 --> 01:15:18,370
Mehmet Bey immediately declared war.

895
01:15:19,550 --> 01:15:20,832
I say all this objectively.

896
01:15:21,286 --> 01:15:27,271
I mean, thank God, even Osman Bey's
stalls are in your market.

897
01:15:27,720 --> 01:15:32,210
It means that the people trust him completely.

898
01:15:32,360 --> 01:15:36,760
- He will stand before the people now...
- Who is Osman in front of Sultan Yakup?

899
01:15:38,100 --> 01:15:40,020
Who is Osman? How dare you?

900
01:15:47,480 --> 01:15:52,660
You say that the people stand behind Osman.

901
01:15:53,615 --> 01:15:58,967
If our market doesn't do well,
and people lose trust...

902
01:16:00,565 --> 01:16:02,769
Osman will take advantage of this?

903
01:16:03,490 --> 01:16:06,830
No, I seek Allah's forgiveness.

904
01:16:08,884 --> 01:16:12,300
I fear Allah.

905
01:16:13,150 --> 01:16:14,980
I love Osman Bey...

906
01:16:15,110 --> 01:16:21,830
this would be slander, and
this body would burn in hell.

907
01:16:23,980 --> 01:16:26,830
I am a trader, my sultan.

908
01:16:27,040 --> 01:16:28,470
My mind doesn't understand.

909
01:16:28,470 --> 01:16:33,280
I'm searching for meaning in
what I know and what I see.

910
01:16:33,420 --> 01:16:36,920
I wanted to consult you on
these meanings.

911
01:16:37,240 --> 01:16:39,870
I don't understand these things.

912
01:16:45,380 --> 01:16:47,430
May I come in, my Sultan?

913
01:16:48,410 --> 01:16:49,470
Come in.

914
01:16:52,600 --> 01:16:55,750
There is an infiltration on
the caged tent, my sultan.

915
01:16:57,210 --> 01:16:58,700
What's going on?

916
01:17:00,810 --> 01:17:02,880
Is it Osman?

917
01:17:06,600 --> 01:17:09,300
We'll find out, Hatun.

918
01:17:26,490 --> 01:17:27,730
Gonca.

919
01:17:28,150 --> 01:17:30,030
These are Byzantine dogs.

920
01:17:30,770 --> 01:17:32,540
They are clearly up to something.

921
01:17:41,430 --> 01:17:44,030
Alps, my Alps.

922
01:17:44,770 --> 01:17:46,600
Who did this, Gonca?

923
01:17:46,770 --> 01:17:49,900
These are not our Alps, father.
They are plotting something.

924
01:17:50,030 --> 01:17:52,010
They were going to kill Alaeddin Bey.

925
01:17:59,200 --> 01:18:03,120
They wanted to kill me and
blame you, Yakup Bey.

926
01:18:04,500 --> 01:18:06,160
Veysel was also one of them.

927
01:18:06,350 --> 01:18:09,990
Even if we search, there's an unknown
traitor among us, my Bey.

928
01:18:10,650 --> 01:18:13,240
I swear I will root them out.

929
01:18:13,670 --> 01:18:15,440
- If necessary, I will...
- Mehmet Bey.

930
01:18:15,590 --> 01:18:18,190
The fruitful tree gets exposed to worms.

931
01:18:18,390 --> 01:18:21,050
But it doesn't stop bearing fruit,
isn't it?

932
01:18:23,350 --> 01:18:25,050
We'll go on our way.

933
01:18:29,760 --> 01:18:31,290
Alaeddin Bey.

934
01:18:31,780 --> 01:18:36,220
Despite your young age,
you have incredible foresight.

935
01:18:37,370 --> 01:18:42,250
I prefer to see you in front of
me instead of Osman Bey.

936
01:18:44,428 --> 01:18:45,908
Yakup Bey...

937
01:18:46,954 --> 01:18:49,092
if you see foresight in me...

938
01:18:49,829 --> 01:18:51,945
know that it is from my father Osman Bey.

939
01:18:55,360 --> 01:19:00,610
Even this statement shows
that I am not wrong.

940
01:19:02,550 --> 01:19:05,040
Please, Alaeddin Bey...

941
01:19:05,400 --> 01:19:07,870
be a guest at my table tonight.

942
01:19:21,901 --> 01:19:27,921
YENIŞEHIR

943
01:19:30,196 --> 01:19:33,457
Fatma, my daughter. Did Aysima come?
Have you seen her?

944
01:19:33,657 --> 01:19:35,259
She was making sweetmeat
in the kitchen, mother.

945
01:19:35,660 --> 01:19:36,360
Okay.

946
01:19:36,700 --> 01:19:38,830
- Mother.
- Yes, Orhan.

947
01:19:39,000 --> 01:19:40,120
Let's talk, mother.

948
01:19:40,250 --> 01:19:43,400
- Come first, Aysima has come.
- Enough, mother.

949
01:19:47,570 --> 01:19:51,654
What do I keep telling you?
And you keep saying Aysima.

950
01:19:51,854 --> 01:19:52,746
Enough.

951
01:19:58,380 --> 01:20:00,280
I won't disturb you.

952
01:20:00,590 --> 01:20:01,850
Excuse me.

953
01:20:03,400 --> 01:20:06,040
Aysima, my daughter.

954
01:20:06,230 --> 01:20:08,040
Go and look, Fatma.

955
01:20:09,620 --> 01:20:12,490
Are you happy with yourself?
You offended the girl.

956
01:20:12,700 --> 01:20:15,450
I didn't do that, you did, mother.

957
01:20:19,380 --> 01:20:21,240
Orhan!

958
01:20:22,410 --> 01:20:24,190
Stop.

959
01:20:24,510 --> 01:20:26,240
What do you think you're doing?

960
01:20:26,430 --> 01:20:28,680
You will apologise to Aysima
immediately tomorrow.

961
01:20:28,830 --> 01:20:33,960
Mother, I try not to overstep
my limit or raise my voice...

962
01:20:34,130 --> 01:20:36,130
- But you don't hear me.
- Orhan!

963
01:20:36,320 --> 01:20:38,240
- Come to your senses.
- I'm in my right mind.

964
01:20:39,750 --> 01:20:41,320
From now on...

965
01:20:41,660 --> 01:20:43,530
I will not say another word on this matter.

966
01:20:44,440 --> 01:20:47,710
I will marry Holofira.

967
01:20:48,550 --> 01:20:50,820
And you will show your consent, mother.

968
01:20:53,680 --> 01:20:57,950
Will you go against your mother's
words for Holofira?

969
01:20:58,400 --> 01:20:59,750
Did I raise you like this?

970
01:20:59,950 --> 01:21:02,816
I'm not the one doing this,
you are.

971
01:21:03,620 --> 01:21:05,254
If you go against my words...

972
01:21:06,888 --> 01:21:09,805
and bring Holofira ti this palace...

973
01:21:10,005 --> 01:21:10,660
Yes, mother?

974
01:21:12,710 --> 01:21:13,600
Come on, say it.

975
01:21:15,150 --> 01:21:16,730
Finish your words.

976
01:21:19,420 --> 01:21:20,550
What are you going to do?

977
01:21:21,480 --> 01:21:23,970
What a shame!

978
01:21:24,970 --> 01:21:27,080
This love has blinded your eyes.

979
01:21:29,080 --> 01:21:30,750
I don't know you anymore.

980
01:21:31,635 --> 01:21:33,028
My son...

981
01:21:33,540 --> 01:21:37,939
wouldn't treat his mother and family
in this way.

982
01:21:38,730 --> 01:21:40,200
I don't want to see you.

983
01:22:04,880 --> 01:22:06,460
They gathered here.

984
01:22:08,150 --> 01:22:09,020
Alps!

985
01:22:11,660 --> 01:22:12,800
Look for traces.

986
01:22:13,170 --> 01:22:14,950
We'll find out which way they went.

987
01:22:15,240 --> 01:22:15,945
Come on.

988
01:22:16,962 --> 01:22:18,150
As you command, my Prince

989
01:22:29,000 --> 01:22:29,710
My Bey.

990
01:22:30,620 --> 01:22:31,710
There are boot tracks.

991
01:22:32,510 --> 01:22:33,710
Turkmen boots.

992
01:22:33,710 --> 01:22:35,710
Their numbers are very large.

993
01:22:37,660 --> 01:22:40,240
Those who have infiltrated us
are even more than we imagined.

994
01:22:40,460 --> 01:22:41,620
That's right, my Bey.

995
01:22:42,680 --> 01:22:44,280
They are plotting things in secret.

996
01:22:44,640 --> 01:22:45,950
Like the Mongols...

997
01:22:46,440 --> 01:22:48,110
they attack secretly.

998
01:22:51,640 --> 01:22:53,020
Shall I tell you a secret, son?

999
01:22:54,240 --> 01:22:59,370
The Mongols and Byzantines began
attacking in a hidden manner.

1000
01:23:00,130 --> 01:23:02,510
They can no longer face us
as they used to before.

1001
01:23:03,550 --> 01:23:06,530
Because we are stronger than them.

1002
01:23:07,750 --> 01:23:08,800
Okay, my Bey.

1003
01:23:25,020 --> 01:23:25,820
Tell me.

1004
01:23:26,000 --> 01:23:28,950
My Bey, we found where
the traces lead to.

1005
01:23:33,220 --> 01:23:34,680
Let's go and get that dog.

1006
01:23:35,060 --> 01:23:36,570
Listen to me carefully now.

1007
01:23:37,550 --> 01:23:40,240
We couldn't do anything about
him following Veysel.

1008
01:23:41,060 --> 01:23:42,170
Okay...

1009
01:23:42,530 --> 01:23:44,040
they have no choice.

1010
01:23:44,150 --> 01:23:45,480
But, father...

1011
01:23:46,040 --> 01:23:50,150
We didn't cut off his head because
he said he would manage on his own.

1012
01:23:50,150 --> 01:23:52,600
And now he says that he
will lead, father.

1013
01:23:52,710 --> 01:23:55,200
He invites the Beys to
take their allegiance.

1014
01:23:55,910 --> 01:23:57,200
Speak, father.

1015
01:23:57,200 --> 01:23:59,200
Who is Osman?

1016
01:24:01,200 --> 01:24:02,860
You will give me permission.

1017
01:24:03,280 --> 01:24:05,460
I will level Yenişehir to the ground.

1018
01:24:05,640 --> 01:24:07,020
And if you don't give me permission...

1019
01:24:07,408 --> 01:24:10,593
I don't care how many men I have,
I will attack that palace, father.

1020
01:24:10,800 --> 01:24:11,680
Mehmet!

1021
01:24:14,080 --> 01:24:18,130
Listen to me so that there is a
difference between you and Osman.

1022
01:24:18,354 --> 01:24:19,759
The time for words is over.

1023
01:24:20,130 --> 01:24:21,550
The swords will speak now.

1024
01:24:22,550 --> 01:24:23,550
Mehmet!

1025
01:24:39,460 --> 01:24:41,800
Go and sit down!

1026
01:24:47,220 --> 01:24:50,660
And attack them like a rabid dog.

1027
01:24:59,600 --> 01:25:00,480
Mehmet.

1028
01:25:01,730 --> 01:25:02,480
Son.

1029
01:25:03,130 --> 01:25:07,400
I leave you a position and a throne.

1030
01:25:08,530 --> 01:25:10,440
Whoever sits on the throne must know.

1031
01:25:12,260 --> 01:25:15,930
If the Sultan draws his sword early...

1032
01:25:17,510 --> 01:25:18,860
he will descend.

1033
01:25:22,280 --> 01:25:25,260
And if the time has come
to draw the sword...

1034
01:25:26,260 --> 01:25:28,080
he does not get his hands dirty.

1035
01:25:34,020 --> 01:25:34,910
Kanyumaz.

1036
01:25:37,510 --> 01:25:40,820
Who knows about the bannerless
withdrawing their pledge from Osman?

1037
01:25:41,060 --> 01:25:42,820
Only Osman knows, my Sultan.

1038
01:25:43,188 --> 01:25:44,854
He didn't announce it out of shame.

1039
01:25:45,800 --> 01:25:47,910
Good.

1040
01:25:49,910 --> 01:25:50,710
Mehmet.

1041
01:25:51,710 --> 01:25:53,640
Send news to the Bannerless.

1042
01:25:55,080 --> 01:25:56,730
Will they strike Osman?

1043
01:25:57,330 --> 01:25:58,730
Not Osman.

1044
01:26:00,150 --> 01:26:05,330
They will strike the Turkmen Beys
whom Osman invited.

1045
01:26:10,280 --> 01:26:12,620
The route of the Beys is known.

1046
01:26:17,570 --> 01:26:18,840
But don't you...

1047
01:26:19,770 --> 01:26:21,240
don't you, Mehmet...

1048
01:26:22,530 --> 01:26:23,820
don't you dare!

1049
01:26:24,220 --> 01:26:29,640
Those Turkmen Beys are my
own flesh and blood.

1050
01:26:30,910 --> 01:26:35,510
Not a single Bey or Alp
will suffer any harm.

1051
01:26:35,750 --> 01:26:40,950
We'll just destroy trust
which Othman earned.

1052
01:26:42,860 --> 01:26:44,880
But we won't kill anyone.

1053
01:26:47,200 --> 01:26:50,570
The Beys will think that Osman
called them to kill them.

1054
01:26:53,820 --> 01:26:55,000
That's right.

1055
01:26:58,420 --> 01:26:59,770
That's right.

1056
01:27:02,632 --> 01:27:05,231
SECRET SITE NEAR KITE

1057
01:27:16,750 --> 01:27:18,710
Greetings.

1058
01:27:19,880 --> 01:27:21,220
Orhan!

1059
01:27:21,420 --> 01:27:23,220
Yes, Orhan.

1060
01:27:23,480 --> 01:27:24,591
How did you find me?

1061
01:27:24,791 --> 01:27:26,770
We followed the smell of your fear.

1062
01:27:28,150 --> 01:27:30,280
And it led to you, Veysel.

1063
01:27:31,260 --> 01:27:36,020
The one who sheds the Turks' blood
cannot run or hide!

1064
01:27:37,110 --> 01:27:39,420
Osman's dogs!

1065
01:27:40,970 --> 01:27:42,330
You've come to your death.

1066
01:27:42,530 --> 01:27:45,373
I will bless your blood with my wrath now.

1067
01:27:48,420 --> 01:27:50,280
Look here!

1068
01:27:51,220 --> 01:27:53,150
Look at this.

1069
01:27:53,660 --> 01:27:57,820
While we were looking for one,
both suddenly came out in front of us.

1070
01:28:01,800 --> 01:28:03,910
You were here too?

1071
01:28:04,730 --> 01:28:05,910
Excellent.

1072
01:28:06,910 --> 01:28:08,480
Let's end this now.

1073
01:28:08,510 --> 01:28:09,910
Wait, Mongol.

1074
01:28:10,550 --> 01:28:11,910
Veysel!

1075
01:28:12,680 --> 01:28:15,240
You won't be able to escape
from this corridor.

1076
01:28:16,000 --> 01:28:17,240
Tooth for tooth.

1077
01:28:17,510 --> 01:28:18,770
Blood for blood.

1078
01:28:18,770 --> 01:28:21,770
We'll see, Osman.

1079
01:28:22,370 --> 01:28:26,040
You will finally meet Vasilis.

1080
01:28:26,480 --> 01:28:28,930
Everyone who knew us is underground.

1081
01:28:29,350 --> 01:28:30,930
You must not know us?

1082
01:28:31,840 --> 01:28:33,660
You will get to know us now.

1083
01:28:34,937 --> 01:28:35,500
Enough!

1084
01:28:35,880 --> 01:28:37,880
Soldiers, attack!

1085
01:28:37,880 --> 01:28:38,950
Come on then.

1086
01:29:23,710 --> 01:29:25,440
I will come back for revenge!

1087
01:29:25,550 --> 01:29:26,460
Come on.

1088
01:29:42,150 --> 01:29:43,400
Veysel!

1089
01:30:19,860 --> 01:30:21,310
Get up. Come on.

1090
01:30:38,600 --> 01:30:39,860
Snarl, you dog!

1091
01:30:40,020 --> 01:30:41,530
Snarl!

1092
01:30:41,710 --> 01:30:43,200
There's no easy death for you.

1093
01:30:43,460 --> 01:30:46,130
Get on your feet, you still
have a price to pay!

1094
01:30:46,364 --> 01:30:50,441
Since you're so in a hurry to
make me pay the price, Osman...

1095
01:30:52,660 --> 01:30:53,710
kill me!

1096
01:30:53,930 --> 01:30:55,530
Let's get this over with!

1097
01:30:55,530 --> 01:30:56,833
Get up.

1098
01:31:01,220 --> 01:31:04,280
With every breath you take,
you will beg for death.

1099
01:31:04,880 --> 01:31:06,150
With every breath.

1100
01:31:27,200 --> 01:31:28,970
The prey has entered the trap.

1101
01:31:29,330 --> 01:31:30,130
Now...

1102
01:31:30,800 --> 01:31:32,840
we'll become hunters and cut them off.

1103
01:31:33,123 --> 01:31:36,352
But Yakup Bey has strict orders.

1104
01:31:36,884 --> 01:31:38,558
None of them will be harmed.

1105
01:31:42,440 --> 01:31:43,260
Come on.

1106
01:31:49,260 --> 01:31:50,770
Alps!

1107
01:31:53,200 --> 01:31:54,950
Defence formation!

1108
01:31:54,950 --> 01:31:56,260
Who are they?

1109
01:31:59,910 --> 01:32:01,800
The Bannerless!

1110
01:32:02,550 --> 01:32:04,940
They pledged allegiance to Osman.

1111
01:32:05,070 --> 01:32:07,960
Why are they attacking us then?

1112
01:32:09,480 --> 01:32:11,070
Turkmen Beys.

1113
01:32:11,230 --> 01:32:15,070
What is this impertinence?

1114
01:32:16,080 --> 01:32:18,210
Does Osman Bey know about this?

1115
01:32:18,300 --> 01:32:20,520
Osman Bey is the one who sent us.

1116
01:32:23,350 --> 01:32:25,790
For the great Turkmen Beys.

1117
01:32:26,100 --> 01:32:28,060
He wanted a great reception.

1118
01:32:28,710 --> 01:32:34,080
Then the field will belong to the Bannerless.

1119
01:32:36,150 --> 01:32:39,360
Osman, how dare you?

1120
01:32:39,890 --> 01:32:41,430
How dare you?

1121
01:32:41,490 --> 01:32:43,840
The order is Osman Bey's.

1122
01:32:43,910 --> 01:32:46,140
Bannerless, strike with your swords!

1123
01:32:48,200 --> 01:32:50,420
Allah is the Greatest!

1124
01:33:13,900 --> 01:33:15,960
Look at me, you masked devil.

1125
01:33:16,220 --> 01:33:18,980
Every time I see your face,
I remember your betrayal.

1126
01:33:19,040 --> 01:33:20,930
Don't test my patience, come on.

1127
01:33:21,550 --> 01:33:23,360
Be grateful you aren't dead, Boran.

1128
01:33:24,570 --> 01:33:25,750
Come on!

1129
01:33:31,690 --> 01:33:33,660
Boran, stop.

1130
01:33:34,240 --> 01:33:35,620
He will live for now.

1131
01:33:37,170 --> 01:33:39,410
My Bey, if this dog lives,
what is the difference?

1132
01:33:39,944 --> 01:33:40,752
Boran!

1133
01:33:41,770 --> 01:33:43,240
He won't die now.

1134
01:33:46,520 --> 01:33:50,610
We won't kill him for revenge,
we'll kill him for Allah's sake.

1135
01:33:55,560 --> 01:33:57,460
We will keep the promise we made.

1136
01:33:58,740 --> 01:34:00,260
We have to take Alaeddin.

1137
01:34:04,650 --> 01:34:05,380
Orhan.

1138
01:34:05,580 --> 01:34:06,300
My Bey.

1139
01:34:06,770 --> 01:34:08,440
Take this dog to the place of exchange.

1140
01:34:08,910 --> 01:34:10,320
Take your brother and come.

1141
01:34:10,540 --> 01:34:11,550
As you command, my Bey.

1142
01:34:12,220 --> 01:34:12,960
Get up!

1143
01:34:13,400 --> 01:34:14,500
Come on!

1144
01:34:15,770 --> 01:34:16,560
Bayındır.

1145
01:34:16,790 --> 01:34:17,740
My Bey.

1146
01:34:17,860 --> 01:34:19,100
Go with them too.

1147
01:34:19,360 --> 01:34:20,510
As you command, my Bey.

1148
01:34:30,930 --> 01:34:32,680
Peace be upon you, Osman Bey.

1149
01:34:33,070 --> 01:34:35,280
Peace be upon you, Dervish Efendi.

1150
01:34:35,850 --> 01:34:37,070
It is Allah's way...

1151
01:34:37,350 --> 01:34:40,410
I was coming to you and
found you on my way.

1152
01:34:42,828 --> 01:34:45,150
You host us every time.

1153
01:34:45,370 --> 01:34:48,080
Please come with us to Yenişehir.

1154
01:34:48,520 --> 01:34:49,850
And sit at our table.

1155
01:34:50,020 --> 01:34:53,790
And the Beys will come too.

1156
01:34:54,000 --> 01:34:55,870
Let's talk a little bit.

1157
01:34:56,620 --> 01:34:58,530
Of course.

1158
01:34:58,940 --> 01:35:00,960
I had something to say...

1159
01:35:01,060 --> 01:35:03,450
I'll say it when we arrive, then.

1160
01:35:03,820 --> 01:35:05,690
Thank you.

1161
01:35:05,880 --> 01:35:06,840
- Boran.
- My Bey.

1162
01:35:06,970 --> 01:35:08,000
Give him a horse.

1163
01:35:08,140 --> 01:35:09,440
Sure, my Bey.

1164
01:35:26,260 --> 01:35:29,700
I will wipe out those who ambush my Beys.

1165
01:35:30,140 --> 01:35:31,390
Bannerless ones!

1166
01:35:31,460 --> 01:35:32,380
Retreat!

1167
01:35:39,030 --> 01:35:40,380
Allah is the Greatest!

1168
01:35:50,730 --> 01:35:52,720
- Yakup Bey.
- Are you okay, Beys?

1169
01:35:52,770 --> 01:35:53,770
Fine, Mr. Jacob

1170
01:35:53,910 --> 01:35:55,940
Praise be to Allah.

1171
01:35:56,060 --> 01:35:57,660
You caught up at the right time.

1172
01:35:57,930 --> 01:35:59,360
If you hadn't come...

1173
01:35:59,500 --> 01:36:01,740
they almost broke our defence.

1174
01:36:01,990 --> 01:36:03,600
Praise be to Allah.

1175
01:36:04,220 --> 01:36:07,000
Weren't those dogs the Bannerless ones?

1176
01:36:07,130 --> 01:36:08,430
They were.

1177
01:36:09,200 --> 01:36:12,480
Didn't they pledge allegiance to Osman?

1178
01:36:12,670 --> 01:36:13,510
They did.

1179
01:36:13,820 --> 01:36:18,690
Well, what Osman Bey get
out of this, Sultan Yakup?

1180
01:36:18,750 --> 01:36:20,820
Isn't it obvious?

1181
01:36:21,210 --> 01:36:23,000
Can't you see?

1182
01:36:23,840 --> 01:36:25,930
Osman wants to become the leader.

1183
01:36:27,260 --> 01:36:29,160
He plots many tricks.

1184
01:36:30,270 --> 01:36:34,280
He wants to eliminate everyone
who stands before him.

1185
01:36:38,930 --> 01:36:42,300
The evidence is clear, Beys,
don't you see?

1186
01:36:43,030 --> 01:36:46,590
Greed is enough to make Osman
plot numerous games

1187
01:36:48,650 --> 01:36:50,630
We'll make him stop.

1188
01:36:52,760 --> 01:36:55,140
We will take revenge for this.

1189
01:36:56,600 --> 01:36:58,650
We will hold him accountable for this.

1190
01:36:59,390 --> 01:37:00,254
We will.

1191
01:37:00,900 --> 01:37:03,300
Osman Bey and his Alps
found Veysel, my Sultan.

1192
01:37:04,460 --> 01:37:06,480
Good.

1193
01:37:07,610 --> 01:37:08,720
And now, my Beys.

1194
01:37:10,440 --> 01:37:12,530
I'll show you the truth.

1195
01:37:14,000 --> 01:37:15,700
We will go to Yenişehir.

1196
01:37:15,860 --> 01:37:19,820
We will learn the truth
from the Osman's Alp.

1197
01:37:21,580 --> 01:37:25,840
We will put an end to Osman's games.

1198
01:37:26,503 --> 01:37:27,393
Come on.

1199
01:37:37,280 --> 01:37:38,430
Have a good day.

1200
01:37:39,610 --> 01:37:41,170
Thank you, Malhun Hatun.

1201
01:37:42,320 --> 01:37:44,480
I want to talk to you, Holofira.

1202
01:37:45,710 --> 01:37:46,670
I'm listening.

1203
01:37:48,890 --> 01:37:50,970
You think I don't like you, don't you?

1204
01:37:52,090 --> 01:37:54,430
It's obvious.

1205
01:37:57,060 --> 01:37:58,580
I like you, my daughter.

1206
01:37:59,640 --> 01:38:02,940
My son loves you, why wouldn't I?

1207
01:38:05,650 --> 01:38:07,930
If Orhan weren't a Bey...

1208
01:38:08,010 --> 01:38:10,460
we'd be talking about your
wedding now.

1209
01:38:12,710 --> 01:38:14,160
But he is a Bey.

1210
01:38:15,450 --> 01:38:18,620
It is his destiny to pursue
his father's dream.

1211
01:38:20,550 --> 01:38:25,040
If you get married, you will
become the Bey's wife.

1212
01:38:25,870 --> 01:38:28,890
You will show the way for all the women.

1213
01:38:32,910 --> 01:38:35,560
Look at these people you don't know.

1214
01:38:40,020 --> 01:38:42,520
Do you think you'll be able to lead them?

1215
01:38:44,890 --> 01:38:46,420
Let's say you can.

1216
01:38:48,400 --> 01:38:54,490
Do you think they will accept a
lady who is not of their religion?

1217
01:38:56,300 --> 01:38:57,500
Is that the problem?

1218
01:38:58,280 --> 01:38:59,520
Is it because I'm a Christian?

1219
01:38:59,680 --> 01:39:01,490
This is not the only problem, my daughter.

1220
01:39:02,570 --> 01:39:05,180
The problem is that you do not know us.

1221
01:39:05,760 --> 01:39:08,180
You do not know our customs and traditions.

1222
01:39:11,230 --> 01:39:13,100
You know about me and Bala, right?

1223
01:39:16,910 --> 01:39:19,310
I married a Bey who
was already married.

1224
01:39:20,540 --> 01:39:24,340
Just to give birth to a child, an heir.

1225
01:39:26,610 --> 01:39:32,320
The day came when we gave up on our
lives and our dreams for this dream.

1226
01:39:32,570 --> 01:39:34,340
We were content with our fate.

1227
01:39:36,040 --> 01:39:37,520
This is the test.

1228
01:39:38,360 --> 01:39:40,640
Let's say you didn't give birth
to a child for Orhan...

1229
01:39:42,060 --> 01:39:44,100
could you make the sacrifice Bala made...

1230
01:39:44,380 --> 01:39:47,080
and consent to Orhan having a second wife?

1231
01:39:48,550 --> 01:39:51,130
For Orhan and the Beylik...

1232
01:39:51,590 --> 01:39:54,000
for this dream we believe in...

1233
01:39:54,540 --> 01:39:57,200
for the sake of all this, are
you willing to risk everything...

1234
01:39:57,440 --> 01:40:00,650
and sacrifice everything
when the time comes?

1235
01:40:03,100 --> 01:40:05,040
I... this...

1236
01:40:05,120 --> 01:40:06,790
I don't hate you, Holofira.

1237
01:40:08,447 --> 01:40:11,730
But I don't think about today,
I think about tomorrow.

1238
01:40:16,830 --> 01:40:18,210
Go from here.

1239
01:40:21,690 --> 01:40:27,400
Don't let Orhan become an enemy to
his mother and father for this reason.

1240
01:40:33,840 --> 01:40:35,930
You will understand me in the future,
my daughter.

1241
01:40:45,120 --> 01:40:47,760
My lady, are you okay?

1242
01:40:55,250 --> 01:40:56,890
You were right, Andra.

1243
01:40:58,960 --> 01:41:01,360
I have no future with Orhan.

1244
01:41:14,350 --> 01:41:15,560
Come on.

1245
01:41:16,970 --> 01:41:18,520
You treacherous dog, come on!

1246
01:41:27,490 --> 01:41:29,020
Get up!

1247
01:41:34,500 --> 01:41:37,080
Come on, walk, dog!

1248
01:41:37,110 --> 01:41:38,610
Walk!

1249
01:41:39,510 --> 01:41:41,470
Wait and see, come on!

1250
01:41:42,150 --> 01:41:45,000
You'll be held accountable for
everything you've done, come on!

1251
01:41:48,630 --> 01:41:51,530
Come on, walk!

1252
01:41:53,920 --> 01:41:55,670
You will not die easily.

1253
01:41:55,730 --> 01:41:57,970
Wait and see, walk!

1254
01:41:58,689 --> 01:41:59,588
Treacherous dog!

1255
01:42:00,060 --> 01:42:03,540
Get up! Get up!

1256
01:42:17,180 --> 01:42:18,956
Come on!

1257
01:42:31,840 --> 01:42:33,060
Mehmet Bey.

1258
01:42:39,630 --> 01:42:42,760
I brought the traitor whom you couldn't hold.

1259
01:42:48,569 --> 01:42:49,655
Release my brother.

1260
01:42:52,979 --> 01:42:54,187
Orhan!

1261
01:42:57,100 --> 01:42:58,060
Alps!

1262
01:42:58,560 --> 01:42:59,980
Take Veysel.

1263
01:43:00,180 --> 01:43:02,380
Stop right there.

1264
01:43:03,610 --> 01:43:05,290
We'll make him talk first.

1265
01:43:11,600 --> 01:43:12,540
Alps!

1266
01:43:13,760 --> 01:43:15,230
Bring Alaeddin.

1267
01:43:24,210 --> 01:43:25,130
Stop.

1268
01:43:59,580 --> 01:44:01,540
Oh, my son.

1269
01:44:01,600 --> 01:44:03,320
Praise be to Allah.

1270
01:44:03,440 --> 01:44:04,780
- I'm fine.
- Praise be to Allah.

1271
01:44:04,810 --> 01:44:06,270
Brother.

1272
01:44:07,640 --> 01:44:08,890
Let me look.

1273
01:44:09,140 --> 01:44:10,010
You're fine, aren't you?

1274
01:44:10,010 --> 01:44:11,040
He is fine.

1275
01:44:11,100 --> 01:44:12,190
Sister.

1276
01:44:12,250 --> 01:44:13,400
Praise be to Allah.

1277
01:44:15,720 --> 01:44:17,030
Speak, Veysel.

1278
01:44:17,140 --> 01:44:18,730
Speak, whose dog are you?

1279
01:44:19,900 --> 01:44:22,870
Who helped you flee the market?

1280
01:44:24,160 --> 01:44:25,810
Why don't you ask Vasilis?

1281
01:44:27,080 --> 01:44:28,600
Maybe he will speak then.

1282
01:44:29,710 --> 01:44:30,800
Isn't it, Vasilis?

1283
01:44:31,790 --> 01:44:35,720
How many names do you have?
How many faces do you have, dog?

1284
01:44:44,120 --> 01:44:45,720
I have many names.

1285
01:44:46,920 --> 01:44:48,970
Which name do you want me to use?

1286
01:44:56,310 --> 01:44:58,440
You are a pawn, Vasilis!

1287
01:44:59,910 --> 01:45:03,870
You are the tongs held by
those scared of the fire.

1288
01:45:09,100 --> 01:45:13,470
I am ancient Rome.

1289
01:45:39,070 --> 01:45:41,500
Vasilis, come on, tell me.

1290
01:45:42,180 --> 01:45:45,800
Who is your master?

1291
01:45:45,890 --> 01:45:47,370
Ancient Rome...

1292
01:45:47,760 --> 01:45:49,620
will come back someday.

1293
01:45:51,260 --> 01:45:55,460
And you won't live to see this.

1294
01:45:55,720 --> 01:45:57,300
I will kill you all.

1295
01:45:57,300 --> 01:45:59,200
- You're going to kill us all?
- Yes.

1296
01:46:08,780 --> 01:46:10,490
You will not die easily!

1297
01:46:10,650 --> 01:46:12,630
You will not die easily!

1298
01:46:18,540 --> 01:46:21,440
YENIŞEHIR

1299
01:46:21,640 --> 01:46:24,270
You honoured us, Dervish Efendi.

1300
01:46:24,270 --> 01:46:26,380
Thank you, Osman Bey.

1301
01:46:29,020 --> 01:46:31,660
We were very tired.

1302
01:46:33,080 --> 01:46:34,720
We suffered a lot.

1303
01:46:35,930 --> 01:46:37,560
We got very angry.

1304
01:46:39,110 --> 01:46:40,590
Let's catch our breath.

1305
01:46:43,580 --> 01:46:45,090
What did our ancestors say?

1306
01:46:45,760 --> 01:46:49,390
He who gets up in anger
always suffers losses.

1307
01:46:52,370 --> 01:46:54,270
Excuse me, Dervish Efendi...

1308
01:46:54,740 --> 01:46:58,510
But Hazret Umar (RA)
was known for his anger.

1309
01:46:58,920 --> 01:47:01,730
The infidels always received
their share of his wrath.

1310
01:47:02,870 --> 01:47:05,800
Don't we always need the same anger?

1311
01:47:08,460 --> 01:47:15,640
If it can be like the anger of Hazret Omar (RA)
and the companions.

1312
01:47:17,560 --> 01:47:19,210
Not for our desires.

1313
01:47:20,620 --> 01:47:26,210
But for the sake of Allah's pleasure.

1314
01:47:27,100 --> 01:47:31,730
Anger with no arrogance nor selfishness.

1315
01:47:33,300 --> 01:47:37,100
Since we mentioned it, let me tell you.

1316
01:47:38,170 --> 01:47:40,110
Let's talk about the companions.

1317
01:47:40,430 --> 01:47:42,170
Do tell us.

1318
01:47:45,294 --> 01:47:47,077
Vasilis, look.

1319
01:47:47,680 --> 01:47:49,760
Look to my eyes.

1320
01:47:51,140 --> 01:47:52,490
Let me tell you a secret.

1321
01:47:53,290 --> 01:47:55,230
Not only to the Byzantium...

1322
01:47:56,320 --> 01:48:00,090
we will march towards the furthest
borders of Rome.

1323
01:48:01,800 --> 01:48:03,310
We'll even surpass it.

1324
01:48:03,480 --> 01:48:06,640
There they will speak our language.

1325
01:48:06,760 --> 01:48:10,300
And they will live according
to our religion there.

1326
01:48:12,040 --> 01:48:16,280
The call to prayer will not stop
in the heart of the crusaders.

1327
01:48:25,620 --> 01:48:27,330
Orhan.

1328
01:48:30,830 --> 01:48:33,630
You are dreaming.

1329
01:48:34,900 --> 01:48:36,370
I will survive from here.

1330
01:48:36,550 --> 01:48:38,200
You'll get out of here, is it?

1331
01:48:38,380 --> 01:48:42,030
I will be your executioner.

1332
01:48:42,463 --> 01:48:43,519
Lift him up.

1333
01:48:44,218 --> 01:48:45,185
Lift him up.

1334
01:48:52,310 --> 01:48:53,505
You baseborn dog!

1335
01:48:55,322 --> 01:48:56,903
I know how to make him talk.

1336
01:48:57,740 --> 01:49:00,450
Alps, take him to the cage tent.

1337
01:49:02,890 --> 01:49:05,510
He will not be unattended until Yakup Bey comes.

1338
01:49:06,990 --> 01:49:08,320
That's right.

1339
01:49:14,940 --> 01:49:16,370
But be careful.

1340
01:49:17,330 --> 01:49:20,020
Don't let them snatch him away
from you again, Mehmet Bey.

1341
01:49:20,460 --> 01:49:23,180
Mind your business, Orhan!

1342
01:49:23,740 --> 01:49:26,760
Orhan, let's go, son.

1343
01:49:29,610 --> 01:49:31,020
Let's go, mother.

1344
01:49:31,720 --> 01:49:32,620
Come on, Alaeddin.

1345
01:49:32,620 --> 01:49:34,310
- Come on, sister.
- Fatma, come on.

1346
01:49:50,950 --> 01:49:53,150
I will wait for you at the market crossroads.

1347
01:49:54,440 --> 01:49:55,380
Okay.

1348
01:50:14,913 --> 01:50:18,094
In the golden era, on the battlefield...

1349
01:50:18,663 --> 01:50:23,103
the Messenger of Allah (PBUH)
pointed to one of the infidels...

1350
01:50:23,830 --> 01:50:29,340
and asked: "Oh Ali, do you want
to fight this infidel?"

1351
01:50:29,980 --> 01:50:33,124
Hazret Ali (RA) said: "Permit me...

1352
01:50:33,775 --> 01:50:37,284
with Allah's grace and will...

1353
01:50:37,591 --> 01:50:42,895
I will save the Muslims from
the evil of this infidel."

1354
01:50:44,770 --> 01:50:47,697
The Messenger of Allah said: "Oh Ali...

1355
01:50:48,285 --> 01:50:53,507
I entrust you to the safety of Allah who
created the earth and the heavens."

1356
01:50:54,780 --> 01:50:58,840
Hazret Ali (RA) went out to the
field and confronted the infidel.

1357
01:50:59,470 --> 01:51:03,180
He invited the infidel to bring faith first.

1358
01:51:04,330 --> 01:51:09,060
When the infidel rejected the invitation,
the fight started.

1359
01:51:09,940 --> 01:51:15,920
After a short while, Hazret Ali (RA) made him
fall to the ground and knelt on his chest.

1360
01:51:16,520 --> 01:51:18,580
He put his sword to his neck.

1361
01:51:19,000 --> 01:51:21,560
He invited him to bring faith again.

1362
01:51:22,440 --> 01:51:26,710
When the infidel understood
that he wouldn't survive this...

1363
01:51:27,020 --> 01:51:29,220
he spat in the face of Hazret Ali (RA).

1364
01:51:32,250 --> 01:51:36,610
Hazret Ali (RA) sheathed his sword
and then rose to his feet.

1365
01:51:38,110 --> 01:51:40,000
The man was surprised.

1366
01:51:40,840 --> 01:51:46,620
He said: "Oh Ali, I spat in your
face to make you angry."

1367
01:51:47,110 --> 01:51:49,560
"So that you kill me immediately
and I may be free."

1368
01:51:49,670 --> 01:51:53,610
"But you sheathed your sword and got up."

1369
01:51:54,160 --> 01:51:56,600
"I don't understand your reason for this."

1370
01:51:57,530 --> 01:52:00,750
Hazret Ali (RA) was silent first.

1371
01:52:02,704 --> 01:52:08,010
Then he looked at his face and said:
"Oh infidel."

1372
01:52:08,860 --> 01:52:12,270
"I didn't kill you right away, I waited."

1373
01:52:12,930 --> 01:52:14,630
"I invited you to bring faith."

1374
01:52:15,650 --> 01:52:20,540
"This is for the sake of Islam
and for the sake of Allah."

1375
01:52:21,650 --> 01:52:24,480
"Then when you spat in my face...

1376
01:52:25,040 --> 01:52:27,210
I took it badly."

1377
01:52:27,510 --> 01:52:36,180
"When this happened I was afraid
I would kill you for myself, not for Allah...

1378
01:52:36,810 --> 01:52:38,980
so I put my sword in its sheath."

1379
01:52:40,970 --> 01:52:45,040
After this, the man said:
"Since you have such good intentions...

1380
01:52:45,190 --> 01:52:52,900
such kindness and benevolence,
your religion is the religion of truth."

1381
01:52:53,900 --> 01:52:59,560
"Show me how to believe and be a Muslim."

1382
01:53:00,530 --> 01:53:03,770
Hazret Ali (RA) told him to say the testimony.

1383
01:53:04,390 --> 01:53:08,230
He said the testimony and became a Muslim.

1384
01:53:08,780 --> 01:53:13,850
He even served Hazret Ali (RA) until his death.

1385
01:53:16,927 --> 01:53:21,767
Now you will say I told
you something again...

1386
01:53:22,872 --> 01:53:25,147
but why this?

1387
01:53:25,640 --> 01:53:31,690
The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) says:
"Actions are according to intentions."

1388
01:53:32,160 --> 01:53:35,160
If your intention is the pleasure of Allah...

1389
01:53:35,460 --> 01:53:39,020
many doors of goodness will open
after your action.

1390
01:53:41,210 --> 01:53:47,010
Who knows, maybe you be the reason
to guide many infidels.

1391
01:53:47,180 --> 01:53:48,280
In Sha Allah.

1392
01:53:49,180 --> 01:53:50,440
In Sha Allah.

1393
01:53:51,000 --> 01:53:53,509
I told you this...

1394
01:53:54,225 --> 01:53:57,367
so that you know that...

1395
01:53:58,160 --> 01:54:02,540
your mercy and anger has value
when it is for the sake of Allah...

1396
01:54:03,550 --> 01:54:05,140
and live according to this.

1397
01:54:07,460 --> 01:54:08,810
Bless your tongue.

1398
01:54:09,240 --> 01:54:11,510
May you live long. Bless your words.

1399
01:54:14,320 --> 01:54:16,150
May I come in, my Bey?

1400
01:54:16,700 --> 01:54:18,060
Come in.

1401
01:54:21,620 --> 01:54:23,000
Peace be upon you.

1402
01:54:23,290 --> 01:54:24,560
Peace be upon you.

1403
01:54:24,560 --> 01:54:28,450
My Bey, there is an important matter.

1404
01:54:32,250 --> 01:54:36,380
No, please be seated.

1405
01:54:44,960 --> 01:54:47,100
- My Bey.
- Tell me.

1406
01:54:48,140 --> 01:54:49,690
They attacked the Beys.

1407
01:54:56,140 --> 01:54:57,500
Who attacked them?

1408
01:54:58,520 --> 01:54:59,290
Who?

1409
01:54:59,470 --> 01:55:01,450
The Bannerless, my Bey.

1410
01:55:02,010 --> 01:55:03,230
What?

1411
01:55:05,850 --> 01:55:08,290
Why would the Bannerless
do something like this?

1412
01:55:10,060 --> 01:55:11,790
Tell me, what happened?

1413
01:55:12,510 --> 01:55:14,220
They said your name, my Bey.

1414
01:55:14,850 --> 01:55:16,640
They attacked them in the
name of Osman Bey.

1415
01:55:16,710 --> 01:55:17,830
What?

1416
01:55:18,280 --> 01:55:21,880
Yakup Bey caught up with them later.

1417
01:55:22,720 --> 01:55:23,700
What?

1418
01:55:25,280 --> 01:55:26,710
Yakup?

1419
01:55:34,730 --> 01:55:37,140
Yakup, huh?

1420
01:55:39,710 --> 01:55:42,630
As long as there is such a Bey...

1421
01:55:43,090 --> 01:55:44,980
what's the need for an enemy?

1422
01:55:45,480 --> 01:55:47,840
He will make me look like
a traitor to the Beys.

1423
01:55:48,930 --> 01:55:50,730
So this is his game.

1424
01:55:51,600 --> 01:55:53,450
So this is his game.

1425
01:55:53,830 --> 01:55:57,250
Now, will they go to the market, my Bey?

1426
01:55:57,800 --> 01:55:58,790
No.

1427
01:56:00,060 --> 01:56:02,430
They will come to us.

1428
01:56:04,680 --> 01:56:06,410
Listen to me carefully.

1429
01:56:12,110 --> 01:56:14,840
I trust you now, deceitful Hatun.

1430
01:56:27,583 --> 01:56:28,507
Schoolboy?

1431
01:56:28,990 --> 01:56:31,130
Welcome, deceitful Hatun.

1432
01:56:31,380 --> 01:56:32,920
Why did you call me here?

1433
01:56:33,230 --> 01:56:34,930
Couldn't you say what you
wanted in the market?

1434
01:56:36,080 --> 01:56:39,450
We haven't raced in a long time.
I thought you missed it.

1435
01:56:40,990 --> 01:56:43,310
What is it? Are you afraid?

1436
01:56:43,480 --> 01:56:44,600
Afraid of you?

1437
01:56:45,500 --> 01:56:48,330
I will defeat you this time, schoolboy,
just saying.

1438
01:56:50,424 --> 01:56:51,199
Okay.

1439
01:56:52,710 --> 01:56:56,160
And you should know that
I will win this race.

1440
01:56:57,730 --> 01:56:59,390
And I'm going to ask something of you.

1441
01:56:59,710 --> 01:57:01,530
Allah Allah, what will you ask for?

1442
01:57:02,030 --> 01:57:03,940
You'll find out when I win.

1443
01:57:06,730 --> 01:57:08,900
We'll go to that hill and come back.

1444
01:57:09,740 --> 01:57:11,110
Whoever gets there first wins.

1445
01:57:11,330 --> 01:57:12,150
Okay.

1446
01:57:12,750 --> 01:57:13,670
Come on then.

1447
01:57:14,310 --> 01:57:15,320
Let's go.

1448
01:57:29,420 --> 01:57:31,710
Come on, deceitful Hatun.

1449
01:57:33,797 --> 01:57:34,695
Come on.

1450
01:57:35,800 --> 01:57:37,910
- Come on!
- Come on!

1451
01:57:54,840 --> 01:57:57,800
Now the Beys will come
towards us with slander.

1452
01:57:57,800 --> 01:57:59,310
They will be angry.

1453
01:57:59,500 --> 01:58:01,080
But we will remain calm.

1454
01:58:01,240 --> 01:58:03,360
Calmness always defeats anger, my Bey.

1455
01:58:03,560 --> 01:58:05,200
As long as they don't cross their limits.

1456
01:58:05,420 --> 01:58:06,830
They will do that too.

1457
01:58:07,070 --> 01:58:08,360
We will show tolerance.

1458
01:58:08,500 --> 01:58:11,070
None of you will draw your
sword without my order.

1459
01:58:12,030 --> 01:58:13,640
Şamil.

1460
01:58:14,700 --> 01:58:16,720
The wind does not calm
down in these lands.

1461
01:58:16,860 --> 01:58:18,540
Tell me, how are things in Shusha?

1462
01:58:18,890 --> 01:58:20,810
All is well in Shusha, my Bey.

1463
01:58:21,060 --> 01:58:23,070
I brought you greetings from Shusha.

1464
01:58:23,400 --> 01:58:24,600
And may peace be upon you.

1465
01:58:25,000 --> 01:58:26,970
We convey our greetings to Shusha too.

1466
01:58:28,330 --> 01:58:29,710
Sure, my Bey.

1467
01:58:29,710 --> 01:58:31,150
We'll see.

1468
01:58:31,630 --> 01:58:37,080
Will peace come to us from the
Beys or misfortunes?

1469
01:58:40,180 --> 01:58:41,240
We'll see.

1470
01:59:06,752 --> 01:59:09,170
Come on, come on.

1471
01:59:11,930 --> 01:59:13,030
Come on!

1472
01:59:13,980 --> 01:59:15,380
- Come on!
- Come on!

1473
01:59:29,750 --> 01:59:32,570
Well, I won this race, deceitful Hatun.

1474
01:59:48,220 --> 01:59:50,170
This is punishment for that training, isn't it?

1475
01:59:50,400 --> 01:59:52,850
You couldn't bear that defeat, schoolboy.

1476
01:59:53,280 --> 01:59:54,460
I don't know.

1477
01:59:55,590 --> 01:59:57,660
Maybe I didn't want to win.

1478
01:59:58,140 --> 01:59:59,610
But today is not the case.

1479
02:00:02,200 --> 02:00:03,900
I needed to beat you today.

1480
02:00:05,610 --> 02:00:07,480
Say, what will you ask?

1481
02:00:07,670 --> 02:00:09,630
You're wondering, aren't you?

1482
02:00:10,220 --> 02:00:11,730
Look, if you play around again,
I swear I'll go.

1483
02:00:11,730 --> 02:00:13,050
You can't go anywhere.

1484
02:00:14,440 --> 02:00:18,510
Since I won the race,
what I say will happen.

1485
02:00:36,280 --> 02:00:40,920
Is this flower yours?

1486
02:00:41,340 --> 02:00:42,640
Why is it with you?

1487
02:00:43,440 --> 02:00:45,350
Answer my question first.

1488
02:00:45,870 --> 02:00:47,440
I'm going.

1489
02:00:48,170 --> 02:00:49,070
Gonca.

1490
02:00:51,770 --> 02:00:52,940
Don't go.

1491
02:00:56,870 --> 02:00:59,360
If you know, why do you ask, schoolboy?

1492
02:01:00,970 --> 02:01:02,320
I want to be sure.

1493
02:01:25,880 --> 02:01:27,190
Actually, you know.

1494
02:01:33,190 --> 02:01:35,710
But you don't trust me, schoolboy.

1495
02:01:36,330 --> 02:01:38,320
I always listened to my mind.

1496
02:01:39,570 --> 02:01:41,480
That's why I always falter.

1497
02:01:43,580 --> 02:01:44,990
But...

1498
02:01:47,390 --> 02:01:48,950
it's such a matter...

1499
02:01:50,930 --> 02:01:52,240
I don't know how to say it.

1500
02:01:53,050 --> 02:01:54,630
I don't know how to say it.

1501
02:02:01,220 --> 02:02:02,310
Gonca.

1502
02:02:04,470 --> 02:02:07,320
Since the first day I saw you...

1503
02:02:10,130 --> 02:02:13,740
my heart screams your name such...

1504
02:02:16,140 --> 02:02:20,810
forget my mind, I don't listen to anyone.

1505
02:02:24,190 --> 02:02:26,200
I can't even hear myself, Gonca.

1506
02:02:28,400 --> 02:02:32,400
I've been wanting to tell you
something for a while.

1507
02:02:35,040 --> 02:02:37,260
I like you, deceitful Hatun.

1508
02:02:53,370 --> 02:02:55,540
You called me, Malhun Hatun.

1509
02:02:56,070 --> 02:02:57,810
Come, my daughter, come.

1510
02:02:58,330 --> 02:03:00,410
My son has something to tell you.

1511
02:03:05,990 --> 02:03:07,230
Orhan Bey.

1512
02:03:09,540 --> 02:03:11,130
Come here a moment.

1513
02:03:29,970 --> 02:03:31,510
Come on, son.

1514
02:03:52,680 --> 02:03:56,290
Forgive me for yesterday,
Aysima Hatun.

1515
02:04:00,870 --> 02:04:02,270
Holofira.

1516
02:04:08,500 --> 02:04:10,350
I always see you upset.

1517
02:04:12,000 --> 02:04:13,660
This does not suit you.

1518
02:04:15,270 --> 02:04:17,950
Your beautiful eyes should always be happy.

1519
02:04:22,750 --> 02:04:24,540
Orhan, don't you dare.

1520
02:04:24,760 --> 02:04:27,030
Mother, let me go!

1521
02:04:27,233 --> 02:04:28,766
I said, don't you dare, Orhan.

1522
02:04:45,500 --> 02:04:50,440
I don't know how to say fancy words.

1523
02:05:00,210 --> 02:05:01,220
I...

1524
02:05:03,200 --> 02:05:05,460
I want to marry you, Holofira.

1525
02:05:08,800 --> 02:05:09,830
Let me go.

1526
02:05:09,850 --> 02:05:12,270
I said, don't you dare.

1527
02:05:31,000 --> 02:05:32,650
My daughter, Aysima.

1528
02:05:33,170 --> 02:05:37,130
Tell your father, it's time to
get to know each other.

1529
02:05:40,920 --> 02:05:42,700
I'll tell him, Malhun Hatun.

1530
02:05:44,870 --> 02:05:46,310
Now, with your permission.

1531
02:05:46,550 --> 02:05:47,650
The stall is unattended.

1532
02:05:49,360 --> 02:05:51,760
Permission is yours, my daughter, you may go.

1533
02:06:00,950 --> 02:06:03,430
This is very sudden, Mehmet Bey.

1534
02:06:05,790 --> 02:06:10,880
If you allow, I want to think about it.

1535
02:06:11,690 --> 02:06:12,840
Of course.

1536
02:06:15,990 --> 02:06:18,260
But accept my gift.

1537
02:06:43,020 --> 02:06:44,430
Then...

1538
02:06:49,690 --> 02:06:53,770
I expect to hear from you,
beautiful Holofira.

1539
02:06:59,920 --> 02:07:02,100
I'll show you beauty now.

1540
02:07:02,550 --> 02:07:03,380
Orhan!

1541
02:07:03,420 --> 02:07:05,080
Enough, Orhan!

1542
02:07:05,080 --> 02:07:05,840
Don't interfere, mother!

1543
02:07:06,040 --> 02:07:07,276
Orhan, I'm talking to you.

1544
02:07:08,460 --> 02:07:10,320
You will disgrace us in front of the people.

1545
02:07:10,550 --> 02:07:12,920
You are a Bey, come to your senses.

1546
02:07:21,030 --> 02:07:23,420
Don't you see Holofira is going her way?

1547
02:07:23,510 --> 02:07:28,280
Don't you understand that
Holofira's way is my way, mother?

1548
02:07:28,670 --> 02:07:31,560
Not now, Orhan.

1549
02:07:46,196 --> 02:07:49,096
YENIŞEHIR

1550
02:08:23,230 --> 02:08:25,500
Welcome, Beys.

1551
02:08:26,060 --> 02:08:28,280
We were not welcome, Osman Bey.

1552
02:08:30,990 --> 02:08:35,110
You tried to make my Beys
bait for the thieves.

1553
02:08:35,900 --> 02:08:40,330
And when you failed,
you receive us armed?

1554
02:08:41,930 --> 02:08:45,660
Whoever comes to the yard like this,
is received in this way, Yakup Bey.

1555
02:08:50,530 --> 02:08:53,640
We thought you were in a
sleep of negligence, Yakup Bey.

1556
02:08:55,070 --> 02:08:59,910
We held our anger because
they deceived you.

1557
02:09:02,220 --> 02:09:07,110
But I see that you are blind to
what you do not want to see...

1558
02:09:08,710 --> 02:09:11,230
and deaf to what you don't want to hear.

1559
02:09:13,370 --> 02:09:14,880
Let's say I'm blind...

1560
02:09:15,840 --> 02:09:17,450
are my Beys blind too?

1561
02:09:20,060 --> 02:09:24,010
They all saw the truth
and they all heard it.

1562
02:09:25,040 --> 02:09:27,130
You ambushed the Beys.

1563
02:09:33,240 --> 02:09:37,990
We wear armour and hold a shield...

1564
02:09:38,850 --> 02:09:42,560
but this does not protect us
from being slandered.

1565
02:09:44,200 --> 02:09:46,670
We have completed our
preparations against the enemy.

1566
02:09:49,340 --> 02:09:51,150
But the enemy amongst us...

1567
02:09:52,810 --> 02:09:55,350
no precaution works against them.

1568
02:09:57,800 --> 02:09:59,350
Good.

1569
02:10:00,080 --> 02:10:02,520
At least you know yourself.

1570
02:10:06,380 --> 02:10:08,910
The Beys trusted you
and took to the road.

1571
02:10:10,470 --> 02:10:12,540
Look at this situation you got them into.

1572
02:10:13,090 --> 02:10:14,810
I know myself very well.

1573
02:10:15,900 --> 02:10:18,820
But I know you too, Yakup Bey.

1574
02:10:21,260 --> 02:10:25,540
Beys, you tell me...

1575
02:10:26,940 --> 02:10:32,720
didn't any of you come forward and say
Osman Bey wouldn't do this?

1576
02:10:33,400 --> 02:10:37,260
Huh? Didn't anyone say this?

1577
02:10:50,830 --> 02:10:52,510
You fall into doubt.

1578
02:10:53,850 --> 02:10:55,260
Your mind is confused.

1579
02:11:01,480 --> 02:11:03,230
But don't worry.

1580
02:11:04,170 --> 02:11:10,040
I will remove all these doubts.

1581
02:11:24,240 --> 02:11:25,330
Alps!

1582
02:11:26,350 --> 02:11:28,250
Close the doors.

1583
02:12:04,230 --> 02:12:06,010
I don't know what to do, Andra.

1584
02:12:06,190 --> 02:12:07,600
We must go immediately!

1585
02:12:07,600 --> 02:12:08,720
Walk!

1586
02:12:09,200 --> 02:12:10,330
What are you doing, Orhan?

1587
02:12:10,330 --> 02:12:11,900
You will think about it, huh?

1588
02:12:12,300 --> 02:12:14,370
- Yes, I will think about it!
- Move away!

1589
02:12:19,230 --> 02:12:21,170
- Leave me!
- Come on, walk!

1590
02:12:22,050 --> 02:12:23,070
What's happening there?

1591
02:12:23,320 --> 02:12:24,350
- Let's go!
- Leave me!

1592
02:12:24,600 --> 02:12:25,620
I said leave me!

1593
02:12:25,620 --> 02:12:27,120
Leave me!

1594
02:12:27,470 --> 02:12:29,720
Get on, come on.

1595
02:12:31,530 --> 02:12:32,220
Orhan?

1596
02:12:32,220 --> 02:12:34,800
I won't listen to any of you
anymore, come on!

1597
02:12:37,650 --> 02:12:38,430
What is this boy doing?

1598
02:12:38,630 --> 02:12:40,064
- Mother.
- He's taking Holofira!

1599
02:12:40,264 --> 02:12:41,440
Orhan!

1600
02:12:48,490 --> 02:12:49,700
Orhan!

1601
02:12:51,788 --> 02:12:52,925
Orhan, stop!

1602
02:12:53,800 --> 02:12:54,830
It's over now!

1603
02:12:55,130 --> 02:12:57,290
I won't listen to any of you!

1604
02:12:57,290 --> 02:12:59,180
You shouldn't have done this, Orhan!

1605
02:13:00,270 --> 02:13:02,560
Alps, to the horses!

1606
02:13:06,530 --> 02:13:08,020
Orhan!

1607
02:13:08,990 --> 02:13:10,080
Orhan!

1608
02:13:11,570 --> 02:13:13,360
We will stop you, Orhan!

1609
02:13:13,580 --> 02:13:14,473
Orhan!

1610
02:13:14,673 --> 02:13:15,396
Mother.

1611
02:13:16,601 --> 02:13:18,160
- Orhan!
- Mother!

1612
02:13:18,655 --> 02:13:19,529
Orhan!

1613
02:13:21,670 --> 02:13:24,350
What have you done, son?
What have you done?

1614
02:13:32,560 --> 02:13:33,900
Mehmet does not have good intentions.

1615
02:13:33,900 --> 02:13:36,160
Come on, go after them!

1616
02:13:39,040 --> 02:13:41,200
Oh Allah.

1617
02:13:42,530 --> 02:13:44,440
Oh Allah, protect my son.

1618
02:13:45,450 --> 02:13:48,080
Come on, come on!

1619
02:13:50,140 --> 02:13:51,470
Come on!

1620
02:13:52,860 --> 02:13:55,260
You set up a big game, Yakup Bey.

1621
02:13:56,090 --> 02:14:00,430
But everyone has a game.

1622
02:14:01,380 --> 02:14:05,260
Until the sword is placed on the neck.

1623
02:14:13,230 --> 02:14:18,610
The trouble you're in will become
bigger than before, Osman Bey.

1624
02:14:19,960 --> 02:14:21,480
While your enemy is one...

1625
02:14:21,940 --> 02:14:24,480
don't make it become ten, Osman Bey.

1626
02:14:31,680 --> 02:14:32,720
Karesi Bey.

1627
02:14:34,410 --> 02:14:37,620
Do you dare to have
me as your enemy?

1628
02:14:38,580 --> 02:14:41,300
What is the meaning of closing
the doors, Osman Bey?

1629
02:14:43,320 --> 02:14:44,730
We will set up the table.

1630
02:14:46,020 --> 02:14:47,480
And we will eat.

1631
02:14:51,600 --> 02:14:56,290
We will talk about everything
we need to talk about.

1632
02:14:56,990 --> 02:14:59,580
Even if we have uninvited guests among us.

1633
02:15:04,190 --> 02:15:06,540
Today the matter will end here.

1634
02:15:07,050 --> 02:15:09,230
My Alps went to fetch the Bannerless.

1635
02:15:10,080 --> 02:15:11,930
Let them come.

1636
02:15:12,290 --> 02:15:17,120
Then we will see who
they took the order from.

1637
02:15:20,640 --> 02:15:22,360
From Yakup Bey?

1638
02:15:25,050 --> 02:15:27,100
Or from Osman Bey?

1639
02:15:34,910 --> 02:15:41,070
You will pay very dearly
for this insolence, Osman.

1640
02:15:44,330 --> 02:15:49,600
You will see what it means
to capture the Sultan.

1641
02:15:50,780 --> 02:15:53,740
Of course there will be a price.

1642
02:15:55,870 --> 02:15:57,820
Let the bannerless come.

1643
02:15:58,400 --> 02:16:00,650
Then we will see what the price is.

1644
02:16:04,300 --> 02:16:05,566
We will see...

1645
02:16:06,791 --> 02:16:07,997
who is a Bey...

1646
02:16:08,432 --> 02:16:09,654
and who is the Sultan.

1647
02:16:19,904 --> 02:16:30,754
Visit turkision.com for more!